- Yes. Thank you. - There are four different kinds.

257
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:05,080
- Thank you, Ms. Yang. - I'll keep all of them to myself.

258
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,680
Give her a hug.

259
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:09,080
- Come over here. - I'm covered in oil. I'm sorry.

260
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,080
- I'm covered in oil. - Don't worry about it.

261
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,720
- You've got this. - We've got this.

262
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:16,690
I was going to just give you these, but I ate your food too.

263
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:18,290
But the food was good.

264
00:10:18,290 --> 00:10:20,730
- Really? - The food tasted good.

265
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:23,790
You should take it seriously when you actually charge people money.

266
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:25,130
- Absolutely. - Always.

267
00:10:25,130 --> 00:10:27,160
- Thank you. - I'll text you, Ms. Yang.

268
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,530
- Okay. - Go home safely.

269
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:32,200
- Go home safely. - Keep up the good work.

270
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,270
Thank you, Ms. Yang.

271
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:35,410
- Make sure to be thorough. - Yes, Ms. Yang.

272
00:10:35,410 --> 00:10:36,770
- We'll be thorough! - Ahk!

273
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:39,480
- Honesty, humility. Ahk. - Ahk!

274
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,650
- Thank you. - Go home safely, Ms. Yang.

275
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:43,250
- Have a great day. Bye. - Thank you.

276
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:44,680
These bandanas are the best.

277
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,350
(The next group of customers enter.)

278
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,820
Oh, my.

279
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,260
Welcome.

280
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,120
Here is the menu for you.

281
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,160
(While Eun Ji takes a new order...)

282
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,960
(The kitchen has cleared all the previous orders.)

283
00:10:57,760 --> 00:11:00,130
(Young Ji doesn't seem to be feeling well.)

284
00:11:00,130 --> 00:11:01,700
Later at break time...

285
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,500
(As a matter of fact, Young Ji...)

286
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,640
Is heartburn also a symptom of burnout?

287
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:11,240
It's possible to get it due to excessive work stress.

288
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,380
We got a new order.

289
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,180
(The examples of work stress)

290
00:11:15,450 --> 00:11:17,650
(On top of that, she has to endure hot steam and smoke.)

291
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:20,890
- Maybe you have an upset stomach. - I don't know. I feel so queasy.

292
00:11:22,990 --> 00:11:24,760
Young Ji, if you're thirsty, drink some sparkling water.

293
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,790
If you're feeling unwell, go sit down for a bit.

294
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,560
I'm fine. I can do this. Please take orders for now.

295
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:33,200
I'm really fine. I'm okay.

296
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:36,300
- How about you go see a doctor? - No. I'm fine.

297
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,970
- You really don't look so good. - I look a bit pale, don't I?

298
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:42,570
Your table number is nine. The cutlery is available upstairs.

299
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,080
(Table 9: Tteokbokki, shrimp burger combo, pizza, carrot cake, ade)

300
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:46,080
You have to be honest about how sick you are, Young Ji.

301
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,280
- Eun Ji is right. - I'm really fine.

302
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,310
- Are you feeling better now? - Yes.

303
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:49,850
Drink some sparkling water.

304
00:11:50,310 --> 00:11:53,320
- We have one shrimp burger to make. - Okay.

305
00:11:53,650 --> 00:11:57,620
(Mimi starts deep-frying a shrimp patty.)

306
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,020
Spray it.

307
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,090
(And then, she oversees the pizza prep.)

308
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:01,730
Nice.

309
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:02,990
(Yu Jin is prepping the pizza.)

310
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:06,930
(She spreads the special sauce evenly.)

311
00:12:07,730 --> 00:12:08,930
The original tteokbokki.

312
00:12:09,470 --> 00:12:11,100
(She grabs a strainer for the sauce.)

313
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,610
- I'll take a quick bathroom break. - Okay.

314
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:16,870
- We have some digestive medicine. - Okay.

315
00:12:16,870 --> 00:12:18,340
(She's taking a quick break in the end.)

316
00:12:18,610 --> 00:12:21,610
- Does she have an upset stomach? - I think so. She ate in a hurry.

317
00:12:23,310 --> 00:12:24,380
I'm worried about her.

318
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,920
(Even though Young Ji is gone for a bit,)

319
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:31,620
(the kitchen keeps on rolling.)

320
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:35,030
(Mimi moves faster to cover for Young Ji.)

321
00:12:35,430 --> 00:12:36,860
(Prepping a full load of tater tots)

322
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:38,800
(Prepping a full load of fried seafood)

323
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,600
(4 glasses of pomegranate ade are ready to go too.)

324
00:12:42,370 --> 00:12:44,200
- Are you okay, Young Ji? - I'm good.

325
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,540
Let me just finish making the tteokbokki real quick.

326
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:47,670
Wait, stop. Take a five-minute break.

327
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:49,370
Table Nine.

328
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:50,410
(Fortunately, Eun Ji buys some time by serving the drinks.)

329
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,610
(Table 9: 4 pomegranate ade)

330
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:55,180
(The shrimp patty is ready too.)

331
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:58,680
(The dishes are coming out without a hitch.)

332
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:01,290
- Rest a bit. Take it easy. - Okay.

333
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:04,320
But let me just finish the tteokbokki. It's on the stove.

334
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,720
Staying here makes me feel more anxious.

335
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:10,090
(It's actually boiling vigorously.)

336
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:14,230
(She turns off the stove.)

337
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,600
Is it okay to keep this as it is?

338
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:20,240
(She sneaks out despite the staff's advice.)

339
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,840
- Sorry. I'll wrap it up real quick. - That's okay.

340
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,010
Don't apologize.

341
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,510
- Don't apologize. - There's no rush.

342
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:28,810
There's no rush.

343
00:13:28,810 --> 00:13:30,050
(The rest of the dishes already came out.)

344
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:31,220
- It's okay. - It's okay.

345
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:33,050
- Everything else is out, right? - Yes.

346
00:13:33,050 --> 00:13:34,250
- Just the tteokbokki is left? - I'll clean up here.

347
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,690
- Yes, just the tteokbokki is left. - For Table Nine.

348
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,820
Hello.

349
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:41,830
Hello. Let me take your order.

350
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:46,200
Young Ji, take your time. It's all pointless if you're sick.

351
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,030
- It's just... Earlier... - The business or whatever.

352
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:51,670
Make me look like a professional psychopath who's sick.

353
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:53,540
We got a new order.

354
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:55,210
Yes.

355
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,710
One non-alcoholic margarita, one ade,

356
00:13:57,710 --> 00:14:00,980
one cake, one shrimp burger combo, and one tteokbokki.

357
00:14:01,450 --> 00:14:02,680
- Let's do this! - Let's do this!

358
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:03,980
Honesty, humility. Aek.

359
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:05,750
Ahk.

360
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:08,120
Is the tteokbokki almost ready?

361
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,120
- It's coming out. - All right.

362
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,990
I feel bad that the tteokbokki came out late.

363
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:14,760
- I'm giving them extra fried sides. - Give them extra fried sides.

364
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,990
I put extra effort into this.

365
00:14:16,990 --> 00:14:19,260
- It's even more beautiful. - Isn't it?

366
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:21,170
- It's even more beautiful. - Thank you.

367
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:22,800
- It's legendary, Young Ji. - I paid extra attention to it.

368
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:25,640
Here's Lee Young Ji's original tteokbokki.

369
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,200
Margarita.

370
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,640
(She walks in cheerfully to make margarita.)

371
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,710
Margarita.

372
00:14:30,610 --> 00:14:31,680
Sparkling water.

373
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:34,780
(She carefully opens the cap.)

374
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:35,780
Here we go.

375
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:36,850
(The sparkling water fizzes over.)

376
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:37,920
Water bomb.

377
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:39,780
Water show.

378
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:44,760
(Eun Ji's enchanting performance)

379
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:48,760
(But there's no one here to watch it.)

380
00:14:50,130 --> 00:14:51,200
(After mixing it well...)

381
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,760
Margarita.

382
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:56,100
(She pours the margarita into a glass with a sugar rim.)

383
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:59,540
The margarita for Table Ten

384
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,770
(With a slice of lemon, it's complete.)

385
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:02,970
Margarita.

386
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:05,340
Try it. It has no alcohol in it.

387
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:06,380
- Thank you. - Thank you.

388
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:11,280
(The earlier wave of customers is heading out.)

389
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:12,950
- Thank you. - Thank you.

390
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:14,990
- Did you enjoy the food? - Yes.

391
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:17,190
- Go home safely. - I liked the tteokbokki the most.

392
00:15:17,190 --> 00:15:18,660
- Goodbye. - Thank you.

393
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:20,490
(The fact that the customers leave 1 by 1 only means...)

394
00:15:20,490 --> 00:15:22,330
(Space Rice Cake)

395
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:24,600
(It only means a new wave is coming!)

396
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,960
Welcome.

397
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:30,270
We love you to space and back. Welcome to Space Rice Cake.

398
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,800
Can I get the name for the reservation?

399
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,270
It's under Kim Jan Di, and I booked for 1pm.

400
00:15:33,570 --> 00:15:35,140
- Ms. Kim Jan Di? - Yes.

401
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:38,880
Almost paradise

402
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:42,280
- Are you adding a pomegranate ade? - Yes.

403
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,710
Understood.

404
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:46,880
Hello. Let me take your order.

405
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:49,220
Is the serving size of tteokbokki big?

406
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,960
It's a good size for 1 to 2 people.

407
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:55,360
- The shrimp burger is ready. - Okay.

408
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:57,330
Is the tteokbokki coming out, Chef Lee?

409
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:59,430
Jung Hye, the tteokbokki is coming right up.

410
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:02,300
I promised to make sure she wouldn't have to work hard like this.

411
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:04,800
You promised me...

412
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,770
I wouldn't even have to lift a finger.

413
00:16:07,870 --> 00:16:09,110
The tteokbokki is ready.

414
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,110
Here's your shrimp burger.

415
00:16:12,810 --> 00:16:14,380
Too much rice cake in a burger

416
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:16,450
Plump shrimp pop

417
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:17,920
(They don't know how to react.)

418
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:20,880
- Thank you. - Thank you. I love you.

419
00:16:21,990 --> 00:16:23,550
Too much rice cake in a burger

420
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:28,430
(This customer is deeply moved and lost for words.)

421
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:30,990
Plump shrimp pop

422
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,060
Please come on up.

423
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:34,300
We serve house-made burgers. It's nice to meet you all.

424
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:35,970
A party of three coming upstairs.

425
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:37,400
- Thank you. - Thank you.

426
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:39,800
A party of three coming upstairs.

427
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:42,870
Byeon Woo Seok, Seo Kang Jun, and Byun Yo Han...

428
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,210
are heading up to the second floor. Thank you.

429
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,880
(Tapping)

430
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:52,280
(However, there's a problem.)

431
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:58,090
(Traces of the previous customers still remain.)

432
00:16:58,490 --> 00:17:01,490
(Here...)

433
00:17:01,490 --> 00:17:04,600
(and there)

434
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:06,160
I'll clean it up for you.

435
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,660
Let me wipe the table.

436
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:10,200
Did you already take your seats? I'm very sorry.

437
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,670
I sincerely apologize once again.

438
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,340
I'm sorry.

439
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:20,080
I'm sorry for making you sit at such a dirty table.

440
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,550
I'll wipe it for you quickly.

441
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:24,450
Gosh, you're very kind.

442
00:17:24,650 --> 00:17:28,790
I wanted to let you know that it's complete mayhem downstairs.

443
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,590
Should I take care of it?

444
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:33,590
- Stay right there, sir. - I'm sorry.

445
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:36,590
How could I make such a valued customer do this?

446
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:38,300
Please stay seated.

447
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,400
- Head Chef. - Yes?

448
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,730
It looks like upstairs isn't getting cleaned properly.

449
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:44,470
- It's mayhem. - Eun Ji.

450
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:46,100
- Yes? - We got a complaint...

451
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:48,410
about the cleaning upstairs.

452
00:17:48,410 --> 00:17:49,510
Oh, my gosh.

453
00:17:49,670 --> 00:17:52,440
You know the middle-aged guy who works part-time...

454
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,280
- for 16 dollars? - Yes.

455
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,780
Would you like him to help you?

456
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:57,410
Tell him to go upstairs now.

457
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:58,950
(Thinking hard)

458
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:01,150
Could he clear 5 tables for 3 dollars?

459
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:02,750
Sixteen dollars is so expensive.

460
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:04,990
(Reluctant to spend the money)

461
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,930
(It's too late to back out. He's coming to work.)

462
00:18:08,190 --> 00:18:10,330
(The middle-aged part-timer comes in.)

463
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:12,130
Too much rice cake in a burger

464
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:14,500
I heard that you were hiring.

465
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,430
Is this the right place?

466
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:18,640
- Could you please clean up? - Yes.

467
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:20,070
Where?

468
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,910
The customers upstairs are finished eating.

469
00:18:22,910 --> 00:18:24,910
But I've never done it before.

470
00:18:24,910 --> 00:18:26,510
I have to learn from Eun Ji.

471
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:27,680
Learn what?

472
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,950
- Cleaning up? - I've only washed dishes.

473
00:18:29,950 --> 00:18:31,420
Take a tray upstairs...

474
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,950
and clear everything off the tables.

475
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:34,650
Give the customers a bright, beautiful smile.

476
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:35,750
- Hurry up. - Where's the tray?

477
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:37,120
You'll find it upstairs.

478
00:18:37,690 --> 00:18:39,860
(After getting pushed out the door, he turns around.)

479
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,630
Shouldn't I wipe the tables?

480
00:18:41,690 --> 00:18:43,260
(She's too busy to answer.)

481
00:18:43,390 --> 00:18:44,800
Yeong Seok, hurry up.

482
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,760
(Laughing)

483
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,070
She told me to clean up.

484
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:50,770
Hello. Thank you.

485
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:52,700
Yu Jin, is there...

486
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:55,070
You'll find a tray. Thank you.

487
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:59,540
(Like his senior told him, he's off to find a tray.)

488
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:03,210
(The youngest member stares into the void.)

489
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:06,480
Hello. It's nice to meet you, our new part-timer.

490
00:19:06,850 --> 00:19:08,390
I didn't learn how to do this.

491
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:10,090
You just need to wipe the table.

492
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,290
Don't I have to spray anything?

493
00:19:11,290 --> 00:19:14,160
Don't worry about that. I'll take care of it at the end.

494
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,890
If you find anything like this, bring it downstairs.

495
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:17,860
- Okay, what about this? - Yes.

496
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:19,400
Just leave it.

497
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:22,700
Is it supposed to be here?

498
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:24,570
Your presence is...

499
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:26,770
making things more complicated.

500
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:29,040
Gosh, it came out really well.

501
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:32,410
- Is that ready to go out? - Just serve honey with it.

502
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:36,250
(She takes some honey and gets ready to head out.)

503
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:39,380
The carrot cake needs to go out.

504
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:43,520
I'm so busy that I can barely think.

505
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:47,460
(She serves the pizza first fast.)

506
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:49,690
Here's your pizza.

507
00:19:49,690 --> 00:19:51,190
Enjoy your food.

508
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:53,030
(Rushing back)

509
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:56,630
(There's so much to do.)

510
00:19:56,830 --> 00:19:58,940
Hello. I'll take your order.

511
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:01,040
- The beef burger is ready. - Okay.

512
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:03,070
I'll take your order.

513
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:05,010
We'd like...

514
00:20:05,110 --> 00:20:06,480
We have another order.

515
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,880
One pomegranate ade, one carrot cake,

516
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:12,850
one pizza, one tteokbokki, and one beef burger, please.

517
00:20:12,850 --> 00:20:13,850
Okay.

518
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:14,950
- Yeong Seok. - Yes?

519
00:20:14,950 --> 00:20:16,690
On your way upstairs,

520
00:20:16,690 --> 00:20:21,160
take tteokbokki and beef burger combo to Table 12.

521
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,530
- Table 12? - Yes.

522
00:20:22,730 --> 00:20:24,560
I'm sorry. You must be disappointed that I'm here.

523
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:25,660
Not at all. I'm happy to see you.

524
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:27,700
They're very busy downstairs.

525
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,470
- Here's your tteokbokki. Enjoy. - Thank you.

526
00:20:29,470 --> 00:20:31,170
(While the new server fills in the gaps)

527
00:20:31,170 --> 00:20:34,340
I should've made a lot of carrot cake earlier.

528
00:20:34,810 --> 00:20:36,210
- Are you ready to order? - Yes.

529
00:20:36,210 --> 00:20:37,370
Too much rice cake in a burger.

530
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:38,640
Two margaritas.

531
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,710
- Okay. - One pomegranate ade.

532
00:20:40,710 --> 00:20:41,750
- That'd be all. - Okay.

533
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:43,110
Isn't Chicago on the menu?

534
00:20:43,110 --> 00:20:46,850
We're discussing whether to add Chicago to the menu or not.

535
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:49,590
I'll do my best to put it on the menu.

536
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,720
Thank you.

537
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,020
(Doing her best immediately)

538
00:20:52,390 --> 00:20:54,420
(I've got six armor)

539
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,090
(You've got a white toothbrush)

540
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:03,900
- Thank you. - Thank you.

541
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:05,970
We have an order.

542
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,770
One pizza, one beef burger,

543
00:21:08,770 --> 00:21:11,740
one carrot cake, two margaritas...

544
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:14,180
Eun Ji, you should get paid for your performance.

545
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,810
- Right. - Why do you keep performing...

546
00:21:15,810 --> 00:21:17,380
without getting paid 9.9 dollars?

547
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:19,280
I just gave them a sneak peek.

548
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,920
How much are we losing because of that?

549
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,050
It was only a sneak peek.

550
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:26,590
(The part-timer is wandering around without knowing what to do.)

551
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,590
We need more side plates.

552
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:30,030
The gray... I mean, the silver ones.

553
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:31,230
(He got it.)

554
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,760
(He's still following orders to a T.)

555
00:21:34,130 --> 00:21:36,500
(Letting the youngest run on autopilot)

556
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,800
Table 12, soda and pomegranate.

557
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:41,640
We're missing glasses for pomegranate ade.

558
00:21:42,170 --> 00:21:44,780
For now, I brought three glasses for pomegranate ade.

559
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:45,780
Where should I put them?

560
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,110
You're so smart.

561
00:21:47,110 --> 00:21:48,650
You brought them out as soon as I asked.

562
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:50,080
Washing dishes is my specialty.

563
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,850
- You're very impressive. - Thank you, thank you.

564
00:21:52,050 --> 00:21:55,750
(Thanks to him, things are slowly coming together.)

565
00:21:56,050 --> 00:21:57,890
This is for Table 11, that's for Table 12.

566
00:21:58,890 --> 00:22:00,160
Do you need help?

567
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:01,860
Please take these to Table 11.

568
00:22:02,690 --> 00:22:05,200
(On the verge of a wrong order disaster)

569
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:06,930
(Table 11, 1 mint carrot cake)

570
00:22:06,930 --> 00:22:08,230
- Your pizza... It's not for you. - No.

571
00:22:08,670 --> 00:22:10,000
- Is this for you? - No.

572
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,470
- They're eating pizza at Table 11. - Carrot cake...

573
00:22:11,470 --> 00:22:13,670
- I'll give you carrot cake first. - Carrot cake is for Table 11.

574
00:22:13,670 --> 00:22:15,370
- This is for another table. - Table 12?

575
00:22:15,370 --> 00:22:16,940
- Please go this way. - Is it Table 12?

576
00:22:17,370 --> 00:22:21,310
- This is our new menu item today. - That's right.

577
00:22:21,310 --> 00:22:23,550
- Could you explain it to them? - It's warm.

578
00:22:24,150 --> 00:22:29,220
Ghost pepper pizza!

579
00:22:31,690 --> 00:22:33,160
(My goodness...)

580
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:36,290
It's made with the hottest peppers...

581
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:39,900
in the world called ghost pepper.

582
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,530
- We ordered one Coke. - Nice to meet you.

583
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:44,570
- Do you want 1 more? - We ordered 1 more.

584
00:22:44,570 --> 00:22:47,240
One more? I'll bring it to you right away. I'm sorry.

585
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,370
- You have to bow at a perfect 90°. - Okay.

586
00:22:49,370 --> 00:22:51,840
We sincerely apologize.

587
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,910
- It's coming right up. - Thank you.

588
00:22:54,950 --> 00:22:56,180
I love you.

589
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:57,750
(1 ghost pepper pizza, 1 mint carrot cake, 1 pomegranate ade)

590
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,550
- I got hungry after sitting here. - Me too.

591
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:00,820
I can smell the food.

592
00:23:00,820 --> 00:23:02,050
Thank you.

593
00:23:02,050 --> 00:23:03,820
(Remaining Order Status)

594
00:23:04,450 --> 00:23:07,290
(Chef Mimi starts with the pizza.)

595
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:10,360
(Making two at the same time)

596
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:13,860
(While she's busy making the pizza)

597
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:16,500
This is insane.

598
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:18,170
These three are insane.

599
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:20,540
(Young Ji's task 1: Tteokbokki)

600
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,770
(Young Ji's task 2: Beef patty)

601
00:23:22,770 --> 00:23:24,540
(Young Ji's task 3: Tater tots)

602
00:23:25,010 --> 00:23:27,510
- Please sprinkle some salt. - Okay.

603
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:28,510
(Seasoning with salt)

604
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:29,780
You're amazing.

605
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:30,850
(Encouraged by Mimi's compliment,)

606
00:23:30,850 --> 00:23:34,280
(she also puts a burger together.)

607
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:35,650
The world I'm living in is...

608
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:37,490
insane.

609
00:23:37,950 --> 00:23:40,560
(Filling the basket with tater tots)

610
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,660
It's hot.

611
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:51,300
(Once it's quickly placed on the tray,)

612
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,370
(Eun Ji finishes making an ade on time.)

613
00:23:54,070 --> 00:23:56,710
- Yes, it's for Table 13. - Okay.

614
00:23:56,910 --> 00:23:58,410
- Hello. - Hello.

615
00:23:58,410 --> 00:23:59,840
- Table 13. - It's for us.

616
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:01,880
This is pomegranate ade.

617
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:03,610
- Thank you. - Enjoy your food.

618
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:06,420
- It came out so fast. - He seems very shy.

619
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:08,250
Right, he got so embarrassed.

620
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,150
Goodness.

621
00:24:10,420 --> 00:24:12,690
I haven't done this before.

622
00:24:12,690 --> 00:24:13,890
(Laughing)

623
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,690
Let me watch you work for a while.

624
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:18,130
How many days have you been working?

625
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,760
My part-time job...

626
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:23,130
I've worked part-time a few times,

627
00:24:23,130 --> 00:24:24,570
- but I never worked regularly. - Really?

628
00:24:24,940 --> 00:24:27,770
Then you should work a few more years before serving margaritas.

629
00:24:27,770 --> 00:24:29,670
Yes, I'd be happy just with cleaning.

630
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,240
You need to work longer.

631
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:32,780
- There's a nice view. - Yes.

632
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:34,810
The house next door has a traditional tiled roof.

633
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:37,810
Who has time to look outside right now?

634
00:24:38,010 --> 00:24:39,720
Go out and ask if customers need anything.

635
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,590
Ask them if they got all their orders.

636
00:24:42,590 --> 00:24:44,390
That part-timer...

637
00:24:44,820 --> 00:24:46,360
We're insanely busy.

638
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:49,060
Why is he looking outside when we're drowning with work?

639
00:24:50,230 --> 00:24:51,430
Is there anything you're waiting on?

640
00:24:51,430 --> 00:24:53,000
We're waiting on our pizza and tteokbokki.

641
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,830
Pizza and tteokbokki? They'll be coming soon.

642
00:24:55,570 --> 00:24:57,000
Hello.

643
00:24:57,730 --> 00:24:59,900
- Did you get everything? - Yes, we got everything.

644
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:02,310
- Did you get everything? - Yes.

645
00:25:02,310 --> 00:25:03,910
- How does it taste? - It's very good.

646
00:25:03,910 --> 00:25:05,310
Do you like it? I'm glad.

647
00:25:05,310 --> 00:25:06,380
(Keeping an eye on him after sending him out)

648
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:07,910
Are you enjoying your food?

649
00:25:07,910 --> 00:25:09,250
Is everything okay?

650
00:25:09,250 --> 00:25:11,410
- The food is great. - Really? I'm glad to hear that.

651
00:25:11,410 --> 00:25:12,580
- Enjoy your food. - Good luck with work.

652
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:15,320
Is this for real?

653
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:16,550
(Feeling dizzy)

654
00:25:16,750 --> 00:25:18,660
- I asked everyone. - What did they say?

655
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:21,990
Some got all their order, and some didn't.

656
00:25:22,190 --> 00:25:23,830
(What did you do?)

657
00:25:23,830 --> 00:25:24,930
- Really? - Yes.

658
00:25:24,930 --> 00:25:27,260
- Gosh, Eun Ji. - You're working hard.

659
00:25:27,430 --> 00:25:29,030
There's some hazing around here.

660
00:25:29,100 --> 00:25:31,500
(Being a middle-aged rookie is rough.)

661
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:33,570
I'm sorry, but could you go upstairs...

662
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:36,240
and check who didn't get this?

663
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:38,170
- Shouldn't I take it with me? - These are pickles.

664
00:25:38,170 --> 00:25:40,040
- Yes, that's a good idea. - Okay.

665
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:43,210
(He trudges upstairs after getting orders from his senior.)

666
00:25:44,050 --> 00:25:45,320
Did you get this?

667
00:25:45,450 --> 00:25:46,680
- No. - You didn't, right?

668
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,980
This is our basic side dish.

669
00:25:48,490 --> 00:25:51,690
Our server Eun Ji probably forgot to serve you.

670
00:25:51,690 --> 00:25:53,460
- Thank you. - Enjoy.

671
00:25:53,660 --> 00:25:55,530
(However...)

672
00:25:55,930 --> 00:26:00,160
(Yuzu radish pickles never made it to the tables.)

673
00:26:00,330 --> 00:26:02,500
Didn't we order two?

674
00:26:03,130 --> 00:26:04,940
- Excuse me, director. - Yes?

675
00:26:05,100 --> 00:26:07,140
We ordered two margaritas,

676
00:26:07,140 --> 00:26:08,610
- but one of them isn't here yet. - Okay.

677
00:26:08,610 --> 00:26:10,470
- I'll go and scold them. - Wait, no...

678
00:26:10,710 --> 00:26:11,740
I'll be right back.

679
00:26:12,080 --> 00:26:15,750
(After realizing Eun Ji's mistake, he walks off with excitement.)

680
00:26:15,980 --> 00:26:17,980
They ordered two margaritas,

681
00:26:17,980 --> 00:26:20,080
but they only got one.

682
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:22,050
- They're complaining a lot. - Which table?

683
00:26:22,050 --> 00:26:24,550
Did you see which number it was?

684
00:26:24,550 --> 00:26:26,090
You're making it very hard for me.

685
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:27,520
Which table is it?

686
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:30,590
It's close to the wall. I didn't check the number.

687
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:32,300
That can happen.

688
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:34,600
Also, it's embarrassing to ask them...

689
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:35,900
about the pickles.

690
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:36,900
- Why? - No one got them.

691
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:39,070
They need to go out now. Come here.

692
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:41,910
Go and serve the pickles to the ones who didn't get them.

693
00:26:41,910 --> 00:26:42,940
Hurry up. Here you go.

694
00:26:42,940 --> 00:26:43,940
- Go. - I'll take this off.

695
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:45,280
- Give me 1 or 2. - Wait.

696
00:26:45,280 --> 00:26:46,810
- Nothing is organized. - Give me 2 or 3.

697
00:26:47,310 --> 00:26:49,210
(Middle-aged man is coming right up.)

698
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:51,450
This is pickled radish that comes with the dish.

699
00:26:51,450 --> 00:26:52,520
Have some when the food gets too greasy.

700
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:53,950
Please have some even if you're almost done.

701
00:26:53,950 --> 00:26:55,190
- We'll eat it as a dessert. - Okay.

702
00:26:55,190 --> 00:26:56,220
Thank you.

703
00:26:56,620 --> 00:26:59,990
(Eun Ji makes the omitted margarita.)

704
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:02,830
(She heads out with the shaker.)

705
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:04,430
Customer Number 14.

706
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:06,500
I apologize for the delay.

707
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:07,900
In front of you...

708
00:27:07,900 --> 00:27:09,830
(My heart fluttered a little)

709
00:27:09,830 --> 00:27:10,870
(Singing)

710
00:27:11,270 --> 00:27:12,570
(Singing)

711
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:15,810
(Intense)

712
00:27:15,970 --> 00:27:17,010
My goodness.

713
00:27:17,010 --> 00:27:18,440
(Her butt was way too close.)

714
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:19,440
(Excuse me)

715
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,440
(And...)

716
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:22,210
(1 person giving her a piercing glare)

717
00:27:22,210 --> 00:27:23,210
Don't look so serious.

718
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:24,210
(Grinning)

719
00:27:24,550 --> 00:27:26,480
(Cheering her on with a forced smile)

720
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:28,590
This should be done. I'm very sorry.

721
00:27:28,590 --> 00:27:29,590
No, it's okay.

722
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:31,150
(Once she fills up the glass)

723
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:33,320
Margarita!

724
00:27:34,090 --> 00:27:35,890
This is Goheung sea margarita.

725
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:37,330
- Thank you. - Senorita.

726
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:38,530
Senorita.

727
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:41,600
- Was that all right? - You're something else.

728
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:44,000
(The kitchen is powering through the last orders.)

729
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:46,400
(Exhausted)

730
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:47,770
We can do this.

731
00:27:48,970 --> 00:27:51,340
This headscarf is too small for me.

732
00:27:52,810 --> 00:27:54,480
- It left a mark on your forehead. - It hurts so much.

733
00:27:55,010 --> 00:27:56,910
(It squeezed her head the entire shift.)

734
00:27:56,910 --> 00:27:57,980
It hurts a lot.

735
00:27:58,180 --> 00:27:59,620
It's not that bad for me.

736
00:27:59,620 --> 00:28:01,420
It's not even coming off of my head.

737
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:03,750
(Gosh, my head...)

738
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:06,390
At this rate, even Ms. Yang would...

739
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:09,490
- understand. - Right.

740
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:11,430
This is our last order.

741
00:28:11,730 --> 00:28:13,330
I'll give more shrimp as you said.

742
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:15,070
That sounds good.

743
00:28:15,670 --> 00:28:20,170
(The last beef burger is also ready.)

744
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:23,740
(And the carrot cake)

745
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:26,280
- Shall we go upstairs together? - Yes, please.

746
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,280
- Okay. - Thank you.

747
00:28:27,340 --> 00:28:29,650
(Heading upstairs with the head chef)

748
00:28:29,650 --> 00:28:31,380
This is great.

749
00:28:31,380 --> 00:28:33,450
- This is the last order. - That's great.

750
00:28:33,550 --> 00:28:34,820
Hello.

751
00:28:35,390 --> 00:28:36,820
(1 original tteokbokki, 1 beef burger combo, 1 mint carrot cake)

752
00:28:36,820 --> 00:28:38,420
- Thank you. - It's really delicious.

753
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,560
Yu Jin made this carrot cake.

754
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:42,060
- Thank you. - Enjoy your food.

755
00:28:42,060 --> 00:28:43,090
Thank you.

756
00:28:43,730 --> 00:28:45,200
(Exclaiming)

757
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:46,930
We gave it everything we had.

758
00:28:46,930 --> 00:28:48,400
(Everyone starts catching their breath.)

759
00:28:48,930 --> 00:28:50,770
I'll have it until tomorrow.

760
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:52,500
(I'll have this mark until tomorrow.)

761
00:28:53,370 --> 00:28:55,040
It comes off when I scrub it immediately.

762
00:28:55,040 --> 00:28:57,340
(Some serious cleanup after the lunch service)

763
00:28:57,640 --> 00:29:01,480
(Eun Ji starts tidying up the dining area.)

764
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,980
(Yu Jin does the final check.)

765
00:29:05,950 --> 00:29:09,420
(Then she suddenly rushes out.)

766
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:13,190
(1 margarita is sitting there in plain sight.)

767
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:14,920
I'm that, I'm that girl

768
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,630
(Our Margarita Girl is just enjoying herself.)

769
00:29:17,890 --> 00:29:19,560
Please let her know that margarita didn't go out...

770
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:20,730
to Table 15.

771
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,130
(The youngest's final run)

772
00:29:24,130 --> 00:29:25,200
(She appears.)

773
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,200
Move out of the way.

774
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,270
- She told me to tell you... - Yes?

775
00:29:27,270 --> 00:29:29,110
that 1 margarita wasn't served to Table 15.

776
00:29:30,510 --> 00:29:32,080
- Do it again and you're in trouble. - Why didn't it go out?

777
00:29:32,580 --> 00:29:35,010
- A margarita didn't go out? - Right, at Table 15.

778
00:29:35,910 --> 00:29:37,310
I sincerely apologize...

779
00:29:37,310 --> 00:29:40,450
for the missed margarita order.

780
00:29:40,450 --> 00:29:43,320
- It's okay. - When a margarita takes this long,

781
00:29:43,350 --> 00:29:45,220
we don't serve it normally.

782
00:29:45,690 --> 00:29:46,720
You don't have to do that.

783
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:49,260
Sure, we'd love to see it.

784
00:29:49,260 --> 00:29:52,460
(Performing after getting permission)

785
00:29:52,730 --> 00:29:55,900
(The kind customers play along.)

786
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,100
(Can you keep up?)

787
00:29:58,270 --> 00:30:00,000
- It should be done. - Thank you.

788
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:02,610
Shall I shake it a little more?

789
00:30:02,610 --> 00:30:03,840
Sure. Yes.

790
00:30:03,970 --> 00:30:07,340
(She starts again right away.)

791
00:30:07,580 --> 00:30:08,610
It's done.

792
00:30:09,050 --> 00:30:10,880
- It wasn't easy. - Thank you.

793
00:30:11,110 --> 00:30:12,650
(The Goheung sea in a glass)

794
00:30:12,780 --> 00:30:14,280
- The color is pretty. - It really is.

795
00:30:18,350 --> 00:30:21,930
(An ending way too dramatic for the performance)

796
00:30:22,190 --> 00:30:23,490
I apologize for the delay once again.

797
00:30:23,490 --> 00:30:25,030
- It's okay. - Don't worry.

798
00:30:25,030 --> 00:30:26,700
- Thank you. - Enjoy.

799
00:30:27,660 --> 00:30:30,430
(Just like that, Eun Ji's gala show is over.)

800
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:31,870
Thank you.

801
00:30:31,870 --> 00:30:32,900
Stay strong.

802
00:30:32,900 --> 00:30:33,970
Thank you.

803
00:30:33,970 --> 00:30:35,070
- I'm coming through. - Bye.

804
00:30:35,070 --> 00:30:36,170
We can do it.

805
00:30:36,170 --> 00:30:39,240
(The customers start to head out 1 by 1.)

806
00:30:39,610 --> 00:30:40,910
- Mi Hyun. - Yes?

807
00:30:41,180 --> 00:30:43,210
I'm getting scared about the dinner service.

808
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:47,080
(The lunch service is over.)

809
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:49,150
Young Ji, I asked for a mat so that you can lie down...

810
00:30:49,150 --> 00:30:50,920
in the pantry, so please wait.

811
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,260
I don't have to lie down.

812
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:55,330
- Come quickly. - I'll be there in a second.

813
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,260
Is your indigestion any better?

814
00:30:59,260 --> 00:31:01,030
I'm losing my mind. I feel like I'm dying.

815
00:31:01,030 --> 00:31:02,230
Seriously?

816
00:31:02,230 --> 00:31:04,700
I feel terrible every time I spray oil.

817
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,840
What about pricking your finger?

818
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:07,970
We just need a needle.

819
00:31:07,970 --> 00:31:09,510
- The old-school finger pricking? - Yes.

820
00:31:09,610 --> 00:31:10,710
That's a good idea.

821
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:12,410
- Have a seat here. - Sit down.

822
00:31:12,410 --> 00:31:14,380
- You'd feel better if I press here. - Start, Young Ji.

823
00:31:14,510 --> 00:31:15,880
- Right? - No.

824
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:18,080
- I don't want to. - Prick this side first.

825
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:19,080
No!

826
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:20,150
Pricking this spot is the most...

827
00:31:20,150 --> 00:31:21,620
- Bring me a needle. - Isn't it effective?

828
00:31:21,620 --> 00:31:22,920
All right.

829
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:25,420
I'll just massage you.

830
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:28,420
(While Young Ji is causing a scene)

831
00:31:28,660 --> 00:31:30,030
(The pantry situation is reported in the production staff group chat.)

832
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:31,360
(We're going to prick Young Ji's finger.)

833
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:32,700
(Come and grab the lancet.)

834
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:34,460
(The first-aid kit is coming to the rescue.)

835
00:31:35,060 --> 00:31:36,870
You got some foundation on.

836
00:31:36,870 --> 00:31:37,870
It's pricked.

837
00:31:37,870 --> 00:31:39,600
- It doesn't hurt, right? - Blood is coming out.

838
00:31:41,770 --> 00:31:44,270
Strangely, I think I feel better...

839
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:45,910
after getting my finger pricked.

840
00:31:46,780 --> 00:31:47,940
Is it just in my head?

841
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:56,120
- Girls, let's go. - Let's do this.

842
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:57,350
We can do it.

843
00:31:57,350 --> 00:31:59,320
Everyone, please wash your hands.

844
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:00,360
Okay.

845
00:32:00,560 --> 00:32:03,230
Try not to splash so much water on the floor.

846
00:32:03,430 --> 00:32:04,430
Okay.

847
00:32:04,430 --> 00:32:06,530
The business never ends.

848
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:09,000
- It's no joke. - Seriously.

849
00:32:09,230 --> 00:32:11,470
Two more days until I become human again.

850
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:13,770
I'm not human right now.

851
00:32:14,070 --> 00:32:15,440
- Young Ji. - Yes?

852
00:32:15,810 --> 00:32:17,140
We set up what you asked for.

853
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:19,280
- What? - Remember what you wanted?

854
00:32:19,380 --> 00:32:20,410
What?

855
00:32:20,410 --> 00:32:21,580
- What did you say? - It's Goheung.

856
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:23,650
(Goheung?)

857
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:25,110
It's the Goheung sea.

858
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:28,180
(It was two days ago.)

859
00:32:28,250 --> 00:32:29,390
Director.

860
00:32:29,390 --> 00:32:32,060
Could you put a seaside background here?

861
00:32:32,060 --> 00:32:33,690
- Behind us? - Yes.

862
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:36,360
- This is seriously... - Right here?

863
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:38,460
stressing me out.

864
00:32:38,460 --> 00:32:39,860
I might get a burnout already.

865
00:32:40,260 --> 00:32:43,070
(Just as the head chef wished, this beautiful view of Goheung)

866
00:32:43,700 --> 00:32:47,270
(Copied and pasted in Seoul)

867
00:32:47,700 --> 00:32:48,970
Thank you.

868
00:32:49,070 --> 00:32:50,440
- Thank you. - To commemorate it,

869
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,940
I'll do a performance.

870
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:54,180
(Want to go see the ocean?)

871
00:32:54,180 --> 00:32:55,750
(Baby)

872
00:32:56,250 --> 00:32:59,920
(Along the seat next to us, down)

873
00:33:00,150 --> 00:33:03,720
(A celebration performance that's exhausting to watch)

874
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:07,460
(I prefer to go to Goheung)

875
00:33:07,460 --> 00:33:08,460
My gosh.

876
00:33:08,790 --> 00:33:10,030
It's Goheung.

877
00:33:10,330 --> 00:33:12,200
What's important is that I don't look this way.

878
00:33:12,830 --> 00:33:14,230
They should've put it on the floor.

879
00:33:14,230 --> 00:33:15,430
I don't look at the floor either.

880
00:33:15,830 --> 00:33:17,570
Could you change this instead?

881
00:33:17,800 --> 00:33:19,670
Draw a picture and paint over it.

882
00:33:19,670 --> 00:33:21,240
(The head chef's field of vision got much narrower.)

883
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:23,210
Yu Jin, can you measure the yuzu dongchimi?

884
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:25,310
- Let's start with the dough. - Okay.

885
00:33:25,940 --> 00:33:27,780
All right, let's do our job.

886
00:33:28,210 --> 00:33:29,980
Do you think we'll miss this moment someday?

887
00:33:30,780 --> 00:33:33,450
Won't it get romanticized with time and become something we miss?

888
00:33:33,450 --> 00:33:35,420
Do you think we'll actually miss this?

889
00:33:36,090 --> 00:33:37,650
When we start missing it,

890
00:33:37,650 --> 00:33:39,290
let's hurry up and do Season Two.

891
00:33:39,890 --> 00:33:41,690
Let's open our third branch.

892
00:33:41,690 --> 00:33:43,390
- It will come true again. - No way.

893
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:45,330
- Who? Me? - Yes.

894
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:48,360
Who else would do it other than you?

895
00:33:49,470 --> 00:33:52,540
Chef, how many days have we been working?

896
00:33:52,540 --> 00:33:54,070
- It's been over a week. - It's been over a week,

897
00:33:54,070 --> 00:33:55,170
and how does it feel?

898
00:33:55,170 --> 00:33:56,370
It feels terrible.

899
00:33:56,510 --> 00:33:58,140
(Her unfiltered and honest response)

900
00:33:58,310 --> 00:33:59,540
What's the hardest part?

901
00:34:00,010 --> 00:34:02,550
It's hardest when I feel like I'm not improving.

902
00:34:02,910 --> 00:34:04,710
You must really love cooking.

903
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:07,620
What about the employees? How are you doing?

904
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,520
It's hard but fun.

905
00:34:09,790 --> 00:34:10,950
Is it fun?

906
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:13,360
(Even she feels awkward saying it.)

907
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:14,860
There's no way this is fun.

908
00:34:15,790 --> 00:34:17,630
If you're having fun doing this, something is seriously wrong.

909
00:34:18,660 --> 00:34:20,060
Go.

910
00:34:20,230 --> 00:34:21,630
While stretching it out...

911
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:24,630
Okay. There it is.

912
00:34:25,500 --> 00:34:26,800
- Two more. - Okay.

913
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:31,910
(The kitchen team prepares the pizza dough.)

914
00:34:32,210 --> 00:34:34,640
(Everyone is focusing quietly on their own work.)

915
00:34:34,640 --> 00:34:36,080
(Laughing)

916
00:34:36,080 --> 00:34:39,280
(Chuckling)

917
00:34:39,650 --> 00:34:40,650
(Smiling)

918
00:34:40,650 --> 00:34:43,020
(A bitter laugh at the endless prep cycle)

919
00:34:43,020 --> 00:34:44,820
(Moaning)

920
00:34:45,290 --> 00:34:47,360
(Screaming)

921
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:49,430
(Screaming)

922
00:34:49,430 --> 00:34:50,960
Do you want to hear how much we made this afternoon?

923
00:34:51,190 --> 00:34:53,160
- How much? - To cheer you up?

924
00:34:53,160 --> 00:34:54,200
- Yes. - Yes.

925
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:55,730
I bet lunch sales were quite good.

926
00:34:55,930 --> 00:34:58,230
- I will tell you. - Including pizzas, right?

927
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:00,140
Today's lunch sales were insane.

928
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:01,740
Let's hear how insane they were.

929
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:04,010
- Lunch sales were 884 dollars. - Gosh.

930
00:35:04,010 --> 00:35:05,140
- My gosh. - That's great.

931
00:35:05,910 --> 00:35:07,240
Let's go for 1,500 dollars.

932
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,110
(Lunch service sales)

933
00:35:09,110 --> 00:35:10,210
(12 beef burger combos, 9 shrimp burger combos,)

934
00:35:10,210 --> 00:35:11,280
(14 original tteokbokki, 10 ghost pepper pizzas,)

935
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:12,350
(14 mint carrot cakes, 7 Goheung sea margaritas...)

936
00:35:12,350 --> 00:35:14,150
(Total lunch sales, 884 dollars)

937
00:35:14,220 --> 00:35:16,650
The biggest seller was...

938
00:35:18,420 --> 00:35:20,320
ghost pepper pizza.

939
00:35:20,560 --> 00:35:22,660
Ghost pepper pizza!

940
00:35:22,660 --> 00:35:24,560
Yes, that's what sold the most today.

941
00:35:24,690 --> 00:35:26,560
(Looking gloomy)

942
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:27,760
That's not the problem.

943
00:35:29,300 --> 00:35:30,730
It's completely burnt. I'm in trouble.

944
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:32,800
I'm sorry.

945
00:35:33,270 --> 00:35:34,940
- It's okay. - I burnt one.

946
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:36,540
I'll eat this for dinner.

947
00:35:37,070 --> 00:35:38,240
Let's eat it together.

948
00:35:38,240 --> 00:35:39,710
Let's make one. I'm hungry.

949
00:35:40,340 --> 00:35:41,840
- What do you think? - Actually, it looks okay.

950
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:43,550
- Yes, let's make one. - You said that it's burnt.

951
00:35:43,550 --> 00:35:44,710
(How does it look okay?)

952
00:35:44,810 --> 00:35:46,020
Should we make one or not?

953
00:35:46,080 --> 00:35:47,350
- Let's make one. - Let's do it.

954
00:35:47,350 --> 00:35:48,480
That sounds good, chef.

955
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:50,350
Let's give it to the part-timer when she comes.

956
00:35:51,820 --> 00:35:54,220
(Peace restored after solving it with staff meal)

957
00:35:54,220 --> 00:35:56,090
- Woman. - Woman, please wait.

958
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:57,230
A human woman.

959
00:35:57,360 --> 00:36:00,830
(During the day, a warm and compassionate woman)

960
00:36:00,930 --> 00:36:02,500
(She doesn't know the luxury of a coffee break)

961
00:36:02,500 --> 00:36:04,370
(A hardworking woman)

962
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:07,700
(When night comes, she preps for dinner and goes to bed)

963
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:09,870
(That kind of hardworking woman)

964
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:11,270
(Lyrics steeped in the joys and hardships of a business)

965
00:36:11,270 --> 00:36:12,910
- I'm a woman - I'm the head chef

966
00:36:13,510 --> 00:36:14,780
(Head chef)

967
00:36:14,780 --> 00:36:17,010
(You're a little rascal)

968
00:36:17,010 --> 00:36:18,080
(The king)

969
00:36:18,080 --> 00:36:19,480
(That's enough. Let's focus.)

970
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:20,980
When is the part-timer coming?

971
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:23,550
- The sauce is ready. - In any minute now.

972
00:36:23,850 --> 00:36:25,020
When the part-timer gets here,

973
00:36:25,020 --> 00:36:26,960
I'll train her.

974
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:28,220
- Okay. - That sounds good.

975
00:36:28,220 --> 00:36:29,790
We're counting on you.

976
00:36:29,860 --> 00:36:31,590
You were showing her who was boss yesterday.

977
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:32,760
During the handover.

978
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,660
How does it go? Too much...

979
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,630
- Too much rice cake in a burger - Too much rice cake in a burger.

980
00:36:36,630 --> 00:36:38,200
Too much rice cake in a burger

981
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:40,470
She was laying down the law with that phrase.

982
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:42,710
I was showing her our energy and spirit.

983
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:45,270
From what I heard yesterday,

984
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:48,380
the person is close to me,

985
00:36:48,380 --> 00:36:51,080
and they're also acquainted with Yu Jin. I have no idea.

986
00:36:51,210 --> 00:36:52,210
Who is it?

987
00:36:52,420 --> 00:36:55,420
The person will add some energy to this exhausted mood.

988
00:36:55,720 --> 00:36:58,090
That's nice. I'm too exhausted now.

989
00:36:59,160 --> 00:37:00,160
It must be here.

990
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:01,560
(Someone has arrived at the restaurant.)

991
00:37:01,560 --> 00:37:02,760
Unbelievable.

992
00:37:04,630 --> 00:37:05,900
(Laughing)

993
00:37:05,900 --> 00:37:06,960
Do I go in?

994
00:37:07,460 --> 00:37:10,330
(Striding straight to the restaurant)

995
00:37:10,570 --> 00:37:14,170
(She enters without hesitation.)

996
00:37:16,210 --> 00:37:17,610
Hello.

997
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:20,010
My goodness.

998
00:37:20,240 --> 00:37:21,980
(They're glad to see her.)

999
00:37:22,110 --> 00:37:23,850
(The savior of exhausted Space Rice Cake)

1000
00:37:24,050 --> 00:37:26,350
(The one-day part-timer is here.)

1001
00:37:26,580 --> 00:37:31,220
(The leader of La Chica, a trendy dance crew)

1002
00:37:31,890 --> 00:37:36,260
(The popular queen who has various charms)

1003
00:37:38,160 --> 00:37:40,760
(Today's part-timer, Gabee)

1004
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:42,900
- Gabee is here. - She's wearing the uniform too.

1005
00:37:42,900 --> 00:37:44,530
- Hello. - How have you been?

1006
00:37:44,530 --> 00:37:46,840
- Hello. - Hello.

1007
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:49,370
- I heard you needed a part-timer. - This is Mimi.

1008
00:37:49,370 --> 00:37:51,210
- She's very busy. - Hello, Mimi.

1009
00:37:51,210 --> 00:37:53,810
- Hello, nice to meet you. - Hello.

1010
00:37:53,810 --> 00:37:56,380
- Sorry, I can't stop halfway. - She has dough to work on.

1011
00:37:56,580 --> 00:37:58,850
- Hello, she's the head chef. - Hello.

1012
00:37:58,850 --> 00:38:00,480
- Hello. - You've become a chef?

1013
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:03,120
- Yes. - Congratulations.

1014
00:38:03,120 --> 00:38:04,190
I can't believe this.

1015
00:38:04,990 --> 00:38:07,520
- Things are very chaotic, but... - Exactly.

1016
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:10,330
- Come here. - We actually run the restaurant.

1017
00:38:10,460 --> 00:38:11,530
I'm sorry in advance.

1018
00:38:11,730 --> 00:38:13,560
I'm sorry, we'll be like this all day long.

1019
00:38:13,700 --> 00:38:16,470
Gabee, we can't say anything when the business starts.

1020
00:38:17,130 --> 00:38:18,530
- We really... - I hope you understand.

1021
00:38:18,530 --> 00:38:20,140
But I really like this kind of work.

1022
00:38:20,140 --> 00:38:22,170
- I like manual labor. - Really?

1023
00:38:22,170 --> 00:38:25,040
- Change with me starting tomorrow. - Even back then,

1024
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:26,140
as I worked at a restaurant, I thought,

1025
00:38:26,510 --> 00:38:28,710
"This is what I should do when I retire."

1026
00:38:28,910 --> 00:38:29,980
Gosh, you said that.

1027
00:38:31,510 --> 00:38:33,520
It took my mind off things.

1028
00:38:34,180 --> 00:38:36,220
- That's right. - She keeps saying dangerous stuff.

1029
00:38:36,220 --> 00:38:38,450
(The birth of another mouth of terror)

1030
00:38:38,790 --> 00:38:41,590
- You're in for trouble. - Thoughts disappeared from my mind.

1031
00:38:44,630 --> 00:38:46,630
(Hurriedly filling up the hole)

1032
00:38:47,130 --> 00:38:49,000
(Looking around)

1033
00:38:49,300 --> 00:38:51,630
Why did you look behind... Did you make another hole?

1034
00:38:51,700 --> 00:38:53,140
(She has no excuse to make.)

1035
00:38:53,270 --> 00:38:54,270
Staff meal again?

1036
00:38:55,140 --> 00:38:56,870
- No. - Come here.

1037
00:38:56,870 --> 00:38:58,170
It's not staff meal at all.

1038
00:38:58,610 --> 00:38:59,980
Don't laugh, Director.

1039
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:01,910
This is what I do for a living.

1040
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:04,250
Please come and make the dough.

1041
00:39:04,250 --> 00:39:05,610
(Making the staff meal with the ruined dough)

1042
00:39:05,950 --> 00:39:07,220
You're making the staff meal already?

1043
00:39:08,250 --> 00:39:09,550
It's good to prepare in advance.

1044
00:39:10,950 --> 00:39:12,660
I won't put special effort into plating.

1045
00:39:13,220 --> 00:39:15,190
Gabee, please try the pizza.

1046
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:18,460
- Thank you. - The plate is really hot.

1047
00:39:18,460 --> 00:39:20,600
- It's spicy. - It's spicy.

1048
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:22,260
- It's spicy. - Be careful.

1049
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:24,100
Do you eat Buldak?

1050
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:26,670
- You bet. - Dip the sauce.

1051
00:39:26,670 --> 00:39:29,140
- It looks delicious. - Be careful, it's hot.

1052
00:39:29,140 --> 00:39:31,540
This is crazy. The dough is so hot.

1053
00:39:31,540 --> 00:39:32,710
It's hot. It's freshly-cooked sticky rice.

1054
00:39:32,710 --> 00:39:33,710
It's so hot.

1055
00:39:33,740 --> 00:39:36,910
(Since it's hot, Eun Ji feeds her.)

1056
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:39,850
(Nodding)

1057
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:43,350
(It makes her eyes open wide.)

1058
00:39:43,350 --> 00:39:44,950
- How is it? - Is it good, Gabee?

1059
00:39:46,390 --> 00:39:47,390
It's so good.

1060
00:39:47,620 --> 00:39:48,790
- Is it good? - Yes.

1061
00:39:48,920 --> 00:39:51,160
- This basil here. - Basil.

1062
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:52,330
This is driving me crazy.

1063
00:39:52,330 --> 00:39:54,600
It's so delicious.

1064
00:39:55,100 --> 00:39:57,930
The rice cake and the dough are different.

1065
00:39:57,930 --> 00:39:59,540
I rolled out the dough.

1066
00:39:59,670 --> 00:40:01,200
(Please compliment me.)

1067
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:03,440
Bits of everyone's soul are in it.

1068
00:40:03,540 --> 00:40:05,340
- It's so delicious. - Thank you.

1069
00:40:05,610 --> 00:40:06,810
It's a pity you're selling a limited amount.

1070
00:40:06,810 --> 00:40:08,010
Exactly.

1071
00:40:08,340 --> 00:40:09,610
You want me to make more?

1072
00:40:09,850 --> 00:40:11,450
(The kitchen team's sharp glares)

1073
00:40:11,450 --> 00:40:13,320
I'm sorry, but may I ask...

1074
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:15,480
what kind of character you are?

1075
00:40:16,220 --> 00:40:17,290
I've lost my mind.

1076
00:40:18,450 --> 00:40:21,060
- I think you can stop now, Mimi. - This is the last one.

1077
00:40:21,060 --> 00:40:23,290
- Should I make one more? - No, let's not do a just-in-case.

1078
00:40:23,390 --> 00:40:24,990
- No. - Is this enough?

1079
00:40:24,990 --> 00:40:27,400
- Don't make it. - Can I really stop?

1080
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:29,730
- Prepare the fritters now. - Okay.

1081
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:37,170
(After acting all cocky, she caused an accident.)

1082
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:39,540
(Patting it)

1083
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:42,040
Do you...

1084
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:44,710
- Mimi. - Give me a second.

1085
00:40:44,710 --> 00:40:46,250
(She left her post for just a second.)

1086
00:40:46,450 --> 00:40:48,750
- I made a mistake. - What?

1087
00:40:49,390 --> 00:40:51,490
I told you.

1088
00:40:51,490 --> 00:40:52,520
I'm sorry.

1089
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:53,620
(Today's lesson: Don't act cocky.)

1090
00:40:54,060 --> 00:40:56,190
- Gabee, you must be busy. - At once.

1091
00:40:56,190 --> 00:40:57,260
- Not at all. - Thanks for coming.

1092
00:40:57,830 --> 00:40:59,860
Anything I can help? I want to do something.

1093
00:40:59,860 --> 00:41:02,500
- What should I hand you? - Shall we gather the energy?

1094
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:04,430
Teach her the honesty humility cheer.

1095
00:41:04,430 --> 00:41:06,800
Honesty, humility, ahk.

1096
00:41:07,240 --> 00:41:08,700
When I say "honesty," you go "honesty."

1097
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:11,140
- Humility, ahk. - Humility, ahk.

1098
00:41:11,140 --> 00:41:12,710
- We literally do it every day. - "Ahk?"

1099
00:41:12,710 --> 00:41:14,840
We're expecting a lot of customers today.

1100
00:41:15,510 --> 00:41:16,850
- To be honest, - The most customers ever.

1101
00:41:16,850 --> 00:41:18,850
if you happen to make a mistake,

1102
00:41:19,150 --> 00:41:21,820
- I might scold you unintentionally. - Of course.

1103
00:41:22,350 --> 00:41:23,350
Gabee.

1104
00:41:24,390 --> 00:41:25,450
Two eyes...

1105
00:41:26,260 --> 00:41:27,360
down.

1106
00:41:28,290 --> 00:41:29,590
- I might do this. - I'm sorry.

1107
00:41:29,590 --> 00:41:31,730
- "Gabee." - So please understand.

1108
00:41:31,730 --> 00:41:32,960
Don't worry.

1109
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:34,030
You know it's nothing personal, right?

1110
00:41:34,030 --> 00:41:36,900
I majored in getting scolded.

1111
00:41:36,900 --> 00:41:38,430
- It's your major? - So don't worry.

1112
00:41:38,430 --> 00:41:39,470
Gabee.

1113
00:41:39,500 --> 00:41:40,600
(Silent)

1114
00:41:40,700 --> 00:41:43,840
Your shoulders down.

1115
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:44,870
(Slumping)

1116
00:41:44,870 --> 00:41:47,540
- That's it. - Can't she lift them up for now?

1117
00:41:47,540 --> 00:41:49,310
- Shall we change it to "up?" - Get them up now.

1118
00:41:49,310 --> 00:41:50,950
- Gabee. - Yes!

1119
00:41:51,410 --> 00:41:53,780
Your shoulders up.

1120
00:41:53,850 --> 00:41:55,320
(Squaring their shoulders)

1121
00:41:55,750 --> 00:41:58,190
- Good. This is perfect. - Scoliosis.

1122
00:41:58,190 --> 00:41:59,520
- Okay. - This is how it goes.

1123
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:01,220
Chef, how many more?

1124
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:03,890
I told you to count. Did you not?

1125
00:42:03,890 --> 00:42:05,360
I told you I can't count.

1126
00:42:05,360 --> 00:42:07,560
What kind of a person in their 20s,

1127
00:42:07,830 --> 00:42:10,000
no, what kind of a 32-year-old cannot count?

1128
00:42:10,200 --> 00:42:12,700
(Oh, dear.)

1129
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:15,970
As I'm grilling next to you, you should count!

1130
00:42:16,610 --> 00:42:19,340
One, two, three...

1131
00:42:19,340 --> 00:42:20,740
I'm sorry to do this with you here.

1132
00:42:20,740 --> 00:42:21,910
It's okay.

1133
00:42:22,040 --> 00:42:24,050
Eleven... I can't even count,

1134
00:42:24,480 --> 00:42:26,520
and how could you embarrass me in front of her?

1135
00:42:27,650 --> 00:42:29,620
- I'm sorry, Mimi. - I forgot how many I counted...

1136
00:42:29,620 --> 00:42:31,990
because I shouted at you.

1137
00:42:32,020 --> 00:42:33,060
(Flustered)

1138
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:35,790
- One, two, three, four... - Eleven, counting the topmost one.

1139
00:42:35,790 --> 00:42:36,990
It's 11 including this?

1140
00:42:37,890 --> 00:42:39,130
(She's going mad because Mimi can't count.)

1141
00:42:39,130 --> 00:42:40,160
Twelve.

1142
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:43,800
(The counting commotion passes.)

1143
00:42:44,100 --> 00:42:46,740
I'll start grilling the buns. Today's business starts.

1144
00:42:46,770 --> 00:42:48,800
(She starts grilling rice cake buns.)

1145
00:42:48,970 --> 00:42:50,970
Gabee, is your album releasing on the 20th?

1146
00:42:50,970 --> 00:42:51,970
Yes, on the 20th.

1147
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:54,140
I read the news that you're releasing an album.

1148
00:42:54,310 --> 00:42:56,810
- Congratulations. - Thank you.

1149
00:42:57,310 --> 00:43:00,320
How did you think to release your own album?

1150
00:43:00,720 --> 00:43:02,820
I should try everything I want.

1151
00:43:02,820 --> 00:43:04,350
- That's life. - How cool.

1152
00:43:04,350 --> 00:43:07,420
- I'm just doing it and enjoying it. - So cool.

1153
00:43:07,820 --> 00:43:09,560
- You only live once. - That's right.

1154
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:11,260
My dear chef wanted to try running a restaurant...

1155
00:43:11,260 --> 00:43:12,900
and is having a burnout now.

1156
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,130
Who are you talking about?

1157
00:43:16,130 --> 00:43:19,070
- Was this your dream, Chef? - I have no idea what you're saying.

1158
00:43:19,070 --> 00:43:20,340
(I have no idea what you're saying.)

1159
00:43:20,600 --> 00:43:23,640
I have a MOT. Do you know what it means?

1160
00:43:24,010 --> 00:43:26,110
- What is MOT? - Mouth of terror.

1161
00:43:26,110 --> 00:43:28,010
- Oh, mouth of terror. - Yes.

1162
00:43:28,010 --> 00:43:29,280
I know what you mean.

1163
00:43:29,280 --> 00:43:30,550
- I know. - In Goheung, she said,

1164
00:43:30,550 --> 00:43:31,780
"I want to go to Seoul."

1165
00:43:32,180 --> 00:43:34,680
"I want to go to Seoul." So we suddenly got dragged here.

1166
00:43:34,680 --> 00:43:36,420
Really? Because she said she wanted to?

1167
00:43:36,420 --> 00:43:37,820
- Yes. - That's scary.

1168
00:43:38,020 --> 00:43:39,690
They make your wish come true.

1169
00:43:39,690 --> 00:43:41,390
They remember everything you said.

1170
00:43:41,390 --> 00:43:43,330
A wish like "I want to earn ten million dollars" don't come true.

1171
00:43:43,830 --> 00:43:45,160
(Current time, 5:30pm)

1172
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:46,230
Are they coming?

1173
00:43:46,230 --> 00:43:48,300
(Current time, 5:30pm)

1174
00:43:49,000 --> 00:43:53,300
(She carefully turns the sign to "open.")

1175
00:43:54,300 --> 00:43:57,140
Come in, everyone.

1176
00:43:58,210 --> 00:44:02,280
(The dinner business starts.)

1177
00:44:03,010 --> 00:44:06,120
(The kitchen team is very serious as usual.)

1178
00:44:06,950 --> 00:44:08,950
(Charismatic)

1179
00:44:09,750 --> 00:44:12,290
- That was cool. - What was?

1180
00:44:12,860 --> 00:44:15,260
- I didn't do anything. - The way you put gijeongtteok in.

1181
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:16,860
- It... - Let's kiss.

1182
00:44:16,860 --> 00:44:18,860
You say that anytime at random.

1183
00:44:18,860 --> 00:44:20,660
She's got issues too.

1184
00:44:20,930 --> 00:44:22,900
(She tries to calm down by kissing.)

1185
00:44:23,270 --> 00:44:26,240
The rice cake's condition is more important than mine.

1186
00:44:27,440 --> 00:44:28,940
That was really cool, wasn't it?

1187
00:44:29,270 --> 00:44:30,840
(Narcissistic)

1188
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:32,310
Are they coming soon?

1189
00:44:33,040 --> 00:44:34,310
(Meanwhile, the new part-timer is excited.)

1190
00:44:34,310 --> 00:44:35,380
I'm curious.

1191
00:44:36,080 --> 00:44:38,580
- Various customers come. - Exactly.

1192
00:44:39,150 --> 00:44:40,680
Were there any moments that got you flustered?

1193
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:42,820
- We can't see anything. - Right.

1194
00:44:42,820 --> 00:44:44,950
The service team... You'll get to experience a lot.

1195
00:44:44,950 --> 00:44:47,490
Me... Oh, is this outfit...

1196
00:44:48,020 --> 00:44:50,490
- for the servers? Okay. - Yes, the service team's uniform.

1197
00:44:50,890 --> 00:44:52,560
Things will be hectic.

1198
00:44:53,230 --> 00:44:54,260
(While the novice part-timer is nervous...)

1199
00:44:54,260 --> 00:44:56,930
- You're starting to feel nervous? - Yes.

1200
00:44:56,930 --> 00:44:58,800
- Hello. - Hello.

1201
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:01,340
We have a new part-timer today too.

1202
00:45:01,340 --> 00:45:03,070
Hello, I'm Gabee.

1203
00:45:03,070 --> 00:45:04,970
Hello.

1204
00:45:04,970 --> 00:45:08,110
I love you as much as the space. Welcome to Space Rice Cake.

1205
00:45:08,110 --> 00:45:10,310
- Love you. - Yes.

1206
00:45:10,310 --> 00:45:11,850
- What's your name? - What's your name?

1207
00:45:11,850 --> 00:45:14,220
- Jeong Eun. - Ms. Kang Jeong Eun.

1208
00:45:14,220 --> 00:45:15,320
What time did you reserve?

1209
00:45:15,420 --> 00:45:18,350
Are you two dating?

1210
00:45:18,350 --> 00:45:20,390
I see, you're two couples on a date.

1211
00:45:20,390 --> 00:45:22,620
It's a double date.

1212
00:45:22,620 --> 00:45:24,330
Oh, my gosh.

1213
00:45:24,330 --> 00:45:26,130
- You guys look so cute. - Yes.

1214
00:45:26,730 --> 00:45:28,130
You're all 19, right?

1215
00:45:28,630 --> 00:45:30,330
- No, I'm 20. - I'm joking.

1216
00:45:30,330 --> 00:45:33,040
No way. I thought you were 19.

1217
00:45:33,100 --> 00:45:36,040
(The servers are very outgoing.)

1218
00:45:36,040 --> 00:45:38,170
Have a look at the menu.

1219
00:45:38,640 --> 00:45:41,340
The pizza was really delicious.

1220
00:45:41,340 --> 00:45:44,210
It's very spicy but delicious. You know what I mean?

1221
00:45:44,210 --> 00:45:46,420
It's super delicious and chewy.

1222
00:45:47,180 --> 00:45:48,720
Since the part-timer has tried it,

1223
00:45:48,720 --> 00:45:51,020
she's recommending the menus too. I like it.

1224
00:45:51,250 --> 00:45:52,890
That means they're ordering a pizza.

1225
00:45:53,390 --> 00:45:56,160
We'll have one each except the soft drinks.

1226
00:45:56,160 --> 00:45:57,990
I understand. You'll change it to an ade?

1227
00:45:58,430 --> 00:46:00,630
You're very witty. You're good.

1228
00:46:00,860 --> 00:46:02,530
(The senior is generous with her praises.)

1229
00:46:02,870 --> 00:46:06,300
Hello. Welcome.

1230
00:46:06,300 --> 00:46:09,440
I love you as much as the space. Welcome to Space Rice Cake. Hello.

1231
00:46:09,440 --> 00:46:11,210
(She copies her senior's greeting right away.)

1232
00:46:11,640 --> 00:46:14,080
(Meanwhile, the puppy eavesdrops on the orders.)

1233
00:46:14,340 --> 00:46:16,450
(A long face)

1234
00:46:17,150 --> 00:46:18,910
I don't welcome them.

1235
00:46:19,580 --> 00:46:20,980
I don't welcome them. Go out.

1236
00:46:21,480 --> 00:46:24,220
Dear viewers. Are you having fun?

1237
00:46:25,020 --> 00:46:26,620
Welcome.

1238
00:46:28,520 --> 00:46:29,830
Why do you act like you welcome them?

1239
00:46:29,830 --> 00:46:31,130
I welcome them wholeheartedly.

1240
00:46:31,460 --> 00:46:33,700
I couldn't welcome them more than this

1241
00:46:34,900 --> 00:46:38,100
One carrot cake which Yu Jin likes,

1242
00:46:38,200 --> 00:46:39,670
one pomegranate ade,

1243
00:46:40,270 --> 00:46:42,270
one margarita,

1244
00:46:42,570 --> 00:46:45,440
one pizza, one tteokbokki,

1245
00:46:45,440 --> 00:46:47,380
one shrimp burger, and one beef burger.

1246
00:46:47,380 --> 00:46:49,140
Okay. Mimi, we have two burgers.

1247
00:46:49,140 --> 00:46:51,180
- Okay. - Another ade.

1248
00:46:51,180 --> 00:46:52,280
(Table 1: Mint carrot cate, 1, pomegranate ade, 2)

1249
00:46:52,280 --> 00:46:54,580
- You can do it. - Here comes the order.

1250
00:46:54,580 --> 00:46:58,220
Two orders of non-alcohol Goheung sea margarita,

1251
00:46:58,220 --> 00:47:01,220
two carrot cakes, two orders of tteokbokki,

1252
00:47:01,220 --> 00:47:04,530
one shrimp burger and one beef burger.

1253
00:47:04,790 --> 00:47:06,830
Oh, gosh. I'm so nervous!

1254
00:47:06,830 --> 00:47:08,660
- You can do it. - You can do it.

1255
00:47:09,230 --> 00:47:12,070
(As learned, she adds pomegranate syrup)

1256
00:47:12,570 --> 00:47:15,640
(Heaps of ice too)

1257
00:47:19,110 --> 00:47:20,210
My gosh.

1258
00:47:20,380 --> 00:47:21,940
It's okay.

1259
00:47:21,940 --> 00:47:23,950
(Sparkling water refreshing enough to explode)

1260
00:47:24,480 --> 00:47:25,910
(Humming)

1261
00:47:29,050 --> 00:47:34,260
(The service master is having international diplomatic ties.)

1262
00:47:35,620 --> 00:47:37,890
This is how things were all this time.

1263
00:47:39,030 --> 00:47:41,900
(They're so used to it.)

1264
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:43,400
She's good.

1265
00:47:44,030 --> 00:47:45,670
She's really good.

1266
00:47:45,930 --> 00:47:48,400
(Her diplomacy is admirable.)

1267
00:47:48,400 --> 00:47:49,710
Here's the order.

1268
00:47:49,710 --> 00:47:51,140
(She proudly enters with the order sheet.)

1269
00:47:51,140 --> 00:47:52,710
I respect you, Eun Ji.

1270
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:55,140
Gabee, you're doing well.

1271
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:57,080
Thank you. I'll do my best.

1272
00:47:57,080 --> 00:47:58,650
- You're cool. - I'll help.

1273
00:47:59,980 --> 00:48:02,880
(Pouring half-wasted sparkling water)

1274
00:48:03,750 --> 00:48:06,620
(The ade is ready.)

1275
00:48:06,620 --> 00:48:08,060
Thank you.

1276
00:48:08,060 --> 00:48:10,630
- I'll serve these two first. - Okay.

1277
00:48:10,930 --> 00:48:13,360
(The experienced server serves first.)

1278
00:48:13,930 --> 00:48:16,430
One... No, two glasses of pomegranate ade.

1279
00:48:17,170 --> 00:48:18,270
One Coke.

1280
00:48:18,930 --> 00:48:20,040
Pickled radish.

1281
00:48:20,400 --> 00:48:22,600
One margarita is on the way.

1282
00:48:23,040 --> 00:48:25,270
It'll be served without trouble.

1283
00:48:26,170 --> 00:48:29,210
- I'll give you nice ones first. - Okay.

1284
00:48:29,210 --> 00:48:30,650
(The rice cake buns are grilled well.)

1285
00:48:31,180 --> 00:48:33,050
Since it's confusing, I'll just give two.

1286
00:48:33,050 --> 00:48:34,480
Okay, just give me two.

1287
00:48:34,650 --> 00:48:36,350
Since you're weak with numbers.

1288
00:48:37,720 --> 00:48:38,920
Thank you.

1289
00:48:39,520 --> 00:48:41,760
- Honesty, humility, ahk. - Ahk.

1290
00:48:41,760 --> 00:48:42,960
(Beef patty enters too.)

1291
00:48:43,260 --> 00:48:45,290
(She starts grilling it seriously.)

1292
00:48:45,930 --> 00:48:47,160
(Press it hard to get the thickness right.)

1293
00:48:47,160 --> 00:48:48,330
Will the beef burger be ready soon?

1294
00:48:48,460 --> 00:48:50,030
- It's on the way. - Yes.

1295
00:48:50,030 --> 00:48:51,630
- Beef is on the way. - Shrimp is ready too.

1296
00:48:51,630 --> 00:48:53,070
I'll serve shrimp burger and beef burger together.

1297
00:48:53,070 --> 00:48:55,040
