1558
00:58:01,850 --> 00:58:03,590
I don't really know him.

1559
00:58:03,590 --> 00:58:04,620
(A brutal mission for the one who hasn't met him)

1560
00:58:04,620 --> 00:58:05,750
Everyone's shy around new people.

1561
00:58:05,750 --> 00:58:07,090
- Mimi, do you want to go? - Right.

1562
00:58:07,090 --> 00:58:08,460
- Okay. I'll get him the drink. - You should go, Mimi.

1563
00:58:08,460 --> 00:58:09,960
Do I hold them like this?

1564
00:58:09,960 --> 00:58:11,060
- Yes. - Yes.

1565
00:58:11,490 --> 00:58:13,360
- I'll be back. - Okay.

1566
00:58:13,360 --> 00:58:14,430
Hello.

1567
00:58:14,600 --> 00:58:15,960
- Hello. - Hello.

1568
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:17,570
- Goodness. - These are on the house...

1569
00:58:17,570 --> 00:58:19,770
- because you taught us. - Thank you.

1570
00:58:19,770 --> 00:58:20,770
- Here. - It's tough, isn't it?

1571
00:58:20,770 --> 00:58:22,600
- No, it isn't tough at all. - Really?

1572
00:58:22,840 --> 00:58:24,340
- Yes. It's been great. - Really?

1573
00:58:24,340 --> 00:58:25,640
You're so pretty.

1574
00:58:25,640 --> 00:58:27,610
- Are you a couple? - No.

1575
00:58:27,840 --> 00:58:29,210
- You're not a couple? - She's our staff.

1576
00:58:29,210 --> 00:58:30,280
- Is that so? - Yes.

1577
00:58:30,380 --> 00:58:32,750
- I hope you have a beautiful time. - Thank you.

1578
00:58:32,750 --> 00:58:33,750
Please give us a second.

1579
00:58:33,750 --> 00:58:35,980
- Young Ji is cooking your dishes. - Okay. Thanks.

1580
00:58:35,980 --> 00:58:37,050
(Served the drinks while wishing them a happy date)

1581
00:58:37,150 --> 00:58:38,290
(At that moment in the kitchen...)

1582
00:58:38,290 --> 00:58:40,490
Young Ji is actually the busiest one.

1583
00:58:40,490 --> 00:58:41,560
She's really busy.

1584
00:58:41,920 --> 00:58:43,660
Goodness, Young Ji.

1585
00:58:43,660 --> 00:58:44,760
(A concerned voice comes from behind.)

1586
00:58:44,760 --> 00:58:45,890
I'm fine.

1587
00:58:46,330 --> 00:58:47,760
- Young Ji. - Yes?

1588
00:58:47,760 --> 00:58:49,260
(Approaching slowly)

1589
00:58:49,260 --> 00:58:51,100
- I'm fine. - Your palms are sweaty.

1590
00:58:51,100 --> 00:58:53,800
- I'm fine. - These weren't transparent before.

1591
00:58:54,270 --> 00:58:56,500
- I'm all good. - Do you need my help?

1592
00:58:56,500 --> 00:58:58,440
- I want to help you. Are you okay? - Thanks to you, Gabee...

1593
00:58:58,740 --> 00:59:00,510
Thanks to you, I feel comfortable.

1594
00:59:00,510 --> 00:59:01,980
You must be having the toughest time.

1595
00:59:01,980 --> 00:59:03,710
- No, it's tough for everyone. - It's crazy.

1596
00:59:04,350 --> 00:59:06,780
Let's be frank. There's one who has to struggle the most.

1597
00:59:06,780 --> 00:59:08,720
- No, everyone is struggling. - Let's be honest.

1598
00:59:08,720 --> 00:59:09,780
No.

1599
00:59:10,390 --> 00:59:11,950
I'm having the hardest time.

1600
00:59:11,950 --> 00:59:14,090
(I'm having the hardest time!)

1601
00:59:14,620 --> 00:59:17,590
Right? You are the one who's facing the hardest time.

1602
00:59:17,830 --> 00:59:18,890
Thanks.

1603
00:59:19,390 --> 00:59:22,160
I told him Young Ji is making delicious dishes.

1604
00:59:22,160 --> 00:59:23,260
They'll be ready in two minutes.

1605
00:59:23,870 --> 00:59:25,370
Let that old guy wait.

1606
00:59:26,670 --> 00:59:28,200
Come and work again tomorrow, Gabee.

1607
00:59:28,640 --> 00:59:31,070
I'm busy tomorrow.

1608
00:59:31,070 --> 00:59:32,440
You're busy tomorrow.

1609
00:59:32,440 --> 00:59:33,540
(Her schedule is too packed to come here again.)

1610
00:59:33,540 --> 00:59:35,440
You wanted detox, though.

1611
00:59:35,440 --> 00:59:37,580
I'm kind of busy tomorrow.

1612
00:59:37,580 --> 00:59:38,880
You have to come.

1613
00:59:38,880 --> 00:59:39,950
(The patty for their teacher is getting grilled.)

1614
00:59:39,950 --> 00:59:43,020
- Let's go. - Let's go.

1615
00:59:43,750 --> 00:59:45,450
- Yes. - Help me with this, Mimi.

1616
00:59:45,450 --> 00:59:46,650
- Yes. - I like it.

1617
00:59:46,650 --> 00:59:48,020
(The most carefully crafted burger is ready.)

1618
00:59:48,020 --> 00:59:49,560
The beef burger is ready.

1619
00:59:49,560 --> 00:59:53,490
Yes. I'll head into the enemy territory myself.

1620
00:59:54,400 --> 00:59:57,330
- Are you going to see Manager Kwon? - Yes. I made the dish.

1621
00:59:57,900 --> 01:00:01,570
It's amazing to meet the chef herself.

1622
01:00:01,570 --> 01:00:03,740
- That's right. - I'm going to set them up...

1623
01:00:03,740 --> 01:00:06,040
- for you to make one trip. - Yes. I'm ready.

1624
01:00:06,040 --> 01:00:07,480
Tteokbokki is ready.

1625
01:00:07,780 --> 01:00:09,210
Okay, Neapolitan Matfia.

1626
01:00:09,210 --> 01:00:10,510
This tteokbokki is mine and mine only.

1627
01:00:10,750 --> 01:00:13,480
- You can take this tray. - Okay. I'll get going.

1628
01:00:13,650 --> 01:00:15,550
- Gosh. That cheap guy. Thanks. - See you.

1629
01:00:16,580 --> 01:00:18,450
(Approaching the cheap guy...)

1630
01:00:18,450 --> 01:00:20,320
(Approaching Manager Kwon resolutely)

1631
01:00:20,560 --> 01:00:21,760
- It's Young Ji. - Hello.

1632
01:00:23,390 --> 01:00:27,960
(The hall is buzzing as the head chef appears.)

1633
01:00:28,360 --> 01:00:32,570
(On her way to her former master, now a customer)

1634
01:00:32,630 --> 01:00:33,670
You asked...

1635
01:00:33,670 --> 01:00:35,300
- for a 1-on-1 face-off. - Who did?

1636
01:00:35,300 --> 01:00:37,010
- I made all of these. - Really?

1637
01:00:37,010 --> 01:00:39,010
I can make them in five minutes now.

1638
01:00:39,010 --> 01:00:40,240
That was really quick, indeed.

1639
01:00:40,240 --> 01:00:41,780
- That was quick, right? - I know.

1640
01:00:41,780 --> 01:00:42,780
Goodness.

1641
01:00:43,310 --> 01:00:44,650
I came myself.

1642
01:00:44,850 --> 01:00:46,750
- You don't serve, then? - Never.

1643
01:00:46,750 --> 01:00:49,120
- You look exhausted. - I'm exhausted.

1644
01:00:49,320 --> 01:00:50,550
- Please enjoy. - Thanks.

1645
01:00:50,550 --> 01:00:51,750
I'll check back on you later.

1646
01:00:52,290 --> 01:00:54,060
- They're all tasty, right? - Yes, they are.

1647
01:00:54,060 --> 01:00:55,590
- It's good, right? - It's good.

1648
01:00:55,590 --> 01:00:57,660
- Where are you from? - We're from China.

1649
01:00:57,660 --> 01:00:58,660
Is it tasty?

1650
01:00:58,660 --> 01:01:00,090
- It's tasty. - Tasty.

1651
01:01:00,090 --> 01:01:02,860
This one has 2 shrimp, but this one has 3.

1652
01:01:02,860 --> 01:01:04,000
I'll get the shrimp.

1653
01:01:04,000 --> 01:01:06,200
(Exposing their mistake by starting a conversation)

1654
01:01:06,570 --> 01:01:08,440
- Mi Hyun. - I think...

1655
01:01:08,440 --> 01:01:10,100
- What did he say? - Hold on.

1656
01:01:10,100 --> 01:01:12,310
The Chinese customers said, "This one has two shrimp,"

1657
01:01:12,310 --> 01:01:13,910
- "but this one has three." - Goodness.

1658
01:01:14,980 --> 01:01:17,710
(While making tteokbokki for the global customers...)

1659
01:01:18,780 --> 01:01:21,150
(Originally, 3 shrimp fries are placed on tteokbokki.)

1660
01:01:21,150 --> 01:01:22,880
They're getting ready. Please wait.

1661
01:01:24,450 --> 01:01:25,750
Tteokbokki is ready.

1662
01:01:25,750 --> 01:01:28,120
(They served it while missing one shrimp fry.)

1663
01:01:28,120 --> 01:01:29,290
(As a result...)

1664
01:01:29,390 --> 01:01:31,490
Why does this one have 3 shrimp while this one has 2?

1665
01:01:32,430 --> 01:01:33,630
File a complaint.

1666
01:01:33,730 --> 01:01:35,860
(The mistake was obvious because they ordered two dishes.)

1667
01:01:36,260 --> 01:01:39,130
(Serving it quickly on a tray)

1668
01:01:39,500 --> 01:01:41,600
(Entering while catching her breath)

1669
01:01:42,070 --> 01:01:43,400
I'm sorry.

1670
01:01:43,400 --> 01:01:46,040
- Thank you. - Thanks.

1671
01:01:46,040 --> 01:01:47,040
- Please enjoy. - Okay.

1672
01:01:47,040 --> 01:01:48,240
- Thanks. - Please enjoy.

1673
01:01:48,510 --> 01:01:50,210
- Are you enjoying it? - Yes.

1674
01:01:50,210 --> 01:01:51,450
Yes. I knew it.

1675
01:01:53,550 --> 01:01:55,180
A chef shouldn't handle it like that.

1676
01:01:55,180 --> 01:01:56,450
We should've done it.

1677
01:01:56,520 --> 01:01:57,720
Let's all go upstairs...

1678
01:01:57,720 --> 01:01:59,420
- and apologize. - I think I served it.

1679
01:01:59,420 --> 01:02:00,590
- Shall we? - Okay.

1680
01:02:00,720 --> 01:02:02,020
We can't do this.

1681
01:02:02,420 --> 01:02:04,930
Gabee, when we cause trouble like this one,

1682
01:02:04,930 --> 01:02:06,360
we bow at a 90-degree angle to apologize.

1683
01:02:06,360 --> 01:02:07,600
Did it happen before?

1684
01:02:07,600 --> 01:02:09,630
You should demonstrate how it's done.

1685
01:02:09,860 --> 01:02:10,930
We're truly...

1686
01:02:10,930 --> 01:02:12,330
- sorry. - Sorry.

1687
01:02:12,330 --> 01:02:14,170
- It's not "My apologies." - We're sorry.

1688
01:02:16,770 --> 01:02:17,870
Look devastated.

1689
01:02:17,870 --> 01:02:19,570
(They have to look devastated.)

1690
01:02:19,770 --> 01:02:22,940
("How to apologize properly" by the floor manager)

1691
01:02:23,850 --> 01:02:25,380
We heard the news...

1692
01:02:25,750 --> 01:02:28,150
that you were missing a piece of the deep-fried shrimp.

1693
01:02:28,880 --> 01:02:32,890
We'll work harder to better serve our customers.

1694
01:02:33,050 --> 01:02:35,290
- We're truly sorry. - Sorry.

1695
01:02:35,660 --> 01:02:38,060
- It's okay. - We're fine.

1696
01:02:38,360 --> 01:02:40,330
- We forgot about it. Sorry. - Yes.

1697
01:02:40,330 --> 01:02:41,960
Then please...

1698
01:02:42,230 --> 01:02:43,460
- enjoy. - Enjoy.

1699
01:02:43,460 --> 01:02:44,700
- Okay. - Okay. Thank you.

1700
01:02:44,700 --> 01:02:46,170
(The lecture on "how to make an apology" ends.")

1701
01:02:46,170 --> 01:02:47,170
Let's go.

1702
01:02:47,840 --> 01:02:49,940
- We always apologize sincerely. - We were sincere.

1703
01:02:49,940 --> 01:02:50,940
We apologize sincerely.

1704
01:02:50,940 --> 01:02:52,570
- We could feel it. - Sincerely.

1705
01:02:53,140 --> 01:02:55,080
They could feel it.

1706
01:02:55,080 --> 01:02:56,780
(A sophisticated apology softened the customers' hearts.)

1707
01:02:56,940 --> 01:02:58,480
I needed to do something, but I forgot about it...

1708
01:02:58,480 --> 01:02:59,880
and went upstairs to mess around.

1709
01:03:00,110 --> 01:03:01,520
- It's okay. - Eun Ji.

1710
01:03:01,520 --> 01:03:02,520
- Yes? - Yes?

1711
01:03:02,520 --> 01:03:04,390
Will you go upstairs...

1712
01:03:04,390 --> 01:03:06,450
and see how Neapolitan Matfia is enjoying the food?

1713
01:03:06,450 --> 01:03:07,520
Okay.

1714
01:03:07,820 --> 01:03:09,160
Check on him later when you serve other dishes.

1715
01:03:09,160 --> 01:03:11,030
- No. I'll go upstairs at once. - Great.

1716
01:03:11,030 --> 01:03:12,960
I think he came with his girlfriend.

1717
01:03:12,960 --> 01:03:14,730
- It looked like a situationship. - It looked like he came...

1718
01:03:14,730 --> 01:03:16,230
with someone he's in a situationship with.

1719
01:03:16,230 --> 01:03:17,370
Of course, they came together.

1720
01:03:17,370 --> 01:03:18,430
- There's something between them. - Exactly.

1721
01:03:18,430 --> 01:03:19,970
- There's definitely something. - I knew it right away.

1722
01:03:19,970 --> 01:03:20,970
- I know. - Is it a situationship?

1723
01:03:20,970 --> 01:03:22,500
- There's something between them. - Really?

1724
01:03:22,500 --> 01:03:24,710
- I'm totally sure. - The lady is all glammed up.

1725
01:03:24,710 --> 01:03:26,510
- She is... - Today...

1726
01:03:26,510 --> 01:03:27,710
It seems she went to a beauty salon.

1727
01:03:27,710 --> 01:03:29,180
- Of course. - Really.

1728
01:03:29,180 --> 01:03:30,650
- He's interested in her. - Yes.

1729
01:03:30,650 --> 01:03:32,050
- It does seem like it. - Also,

1730
01:03:32,050 --> 01:03:33,780
do you know what made it more obvious?

1731
01:03:33,780 --> 01:03:36,850
He was strangely nicer to me than usual.

1732
01:03:37,390 --> 01:03:39,250
I'm the manager here in charge of developing new dishes.

1733
01:03:39,620 --> 01:03:40,620
(I'm the manager here in charge of developing new dishes.)

1734
01:03:40,620 --> 01:03:42,790
How could they do so well when I taught them only once?

1735
01:03:43,760 --> 01:03:45,130
It must be really tough.

1736
01:03:46,830 --> 01:03:50,530
(He's strangely different.)

1737
01:03:51,000 --> 01:03:52,470
- What? - He's oddly nice to me.

1738
01:03:52,470 --> 01:03:53,470
Why?

1739
01:03:53,470 --> 01:03:55,270
- I don't know. - Usually, he's not that nice to me.

1740
01:03:56,400 --> 01:03:58,870
Really? Did he really do that?

1741
01:03:59,110 --> 01:04:01,280
(Tell me more)

1742
01:04:01,280 --> 01:04:02,540
(Hurry and tell me)

1743
01:04:03,080 --> 01:04:04,710
(And the lady)

1744
01:04:05,050 --> 01:04:07,350
(It seemed like she went to a salon)

1745
01:04:07,650 --> 01:04:10,450
(So I knew they were in a situationship)

1746
01:04:10,690 --> 01:04:11,790
(Singing)

1747
01:04:11,950 --> 01:04:13,820
(I have to continue)

1748
01:04:14,560 --> 01:04:15,760
(But I have nothing more to say)

1749
01:04:15,820 --> 01:04:16,820
(Upstairs in the meantime)

1750
01:04:16,820 --> 01:04:18,090
- I'll cut it in half. - Okay.

1751
01:04:19,260 --> 01:04:22,360
(It looks like he's cutting steak when it's a burger.)

1752
01:04:22,430 --> 01:04:24,730
Cutting a burger isn't easy. You know that, right?

1753
01:04:24,730 --> 01:04:26,500
The patty is well-shaped and nicely grilled.

1754
01:04:27,440 --> 01:04:29,200
- You have to cut it like this. - Thanks.

1755
01:04:29,200 --> 01:04:30,570
(Sharing the beef burger in a sweet manner)

1756
01:04:31,040 --> 01:04:33,110
- I'm more curious about tteokbokki. - Let's try it.

1757
01:04:33,470 --> 01:04:36,380
(He tries a bite of tteokbokki in a cozy manner.)

1758
01:04:38,080 --> 01:04:39,180
(Satisfied)

1759
01:04:39,180 --> 01:04:40,250
It's good.

1760
01:04:41,380 --> 01:04:43,850
It's working up my appetite. That's not good. It's an emergency.

1761
01:04:44,220 --> 01:04:47,390
(Tteokbokki that increases both appetite and love)

1762
01:04:47,690 --> 01:04:49,390
I didn't order a lot on purpose...

1763
01:04:50,490 --> 01:04:51,660
in case they don't taste good.

1764
01:04:52,330 --> 01:04:54,200
- But it's good. - It's tasty.

1765
01:04:54,200 --> 01:04:55,330
(He was afraid of their skills to order a lot.)

1766
01:04:55,330 --> 01:04:56,500
I should've ordered more.

1767
01:04:57,600 --> 01:05:01,340
(Next, he tries the beef burger.)

1768
01:05:01,340 --> 01:05:02,670
(Surprised)

1769
01:05:03,040 --> 01:05:04,710
- It's good. - Why does it taste good?

1770
01:05:05,270 --> 01:05:06,270
It's really good.

1771
01:05:06,270 --> 01:05:09,280
(Taking a big bite while whipping around his piercings)

1772
01:05:09,510 --> 01:05:11,150
I need to recruit Young Ji and Mimi...

1773
01:05:11,880 --> 01:05:12,980
to work at my restaurant.

1774
01:05:13,250 --> 01:05:16,720
(Manager Kwon won both love and students.)

1775
01:05:16,820 --> 01:05:18,190
- I feel really good. - Gabee.

1776
01:05:18,190 --> 01:05:20,190
- We had great reviews. - You should take a break, Gabee.

1777
01:05:20,190 --> 01:05:22,760
- No. I'm feeling great. - You need some rest.

1778
01:05:22,760 --> 01:05:24,260
- Actually, - Take some rest, Gabee.

1779
01:05:24,260 --> 01:05:26,290
- I'm waiting for something. - For what?

1780
01:05:26,930 --> 01:05:28,530
I want to try some. I'm just saying.

1781
01:05:31,570 --> 01:05:33,830
No. I know you're busy.

1782
01:05:33,830 --> 01:05:34,970
- I don't need to try it. - Okay.

1783
01:05:34,970 --> 01:05:36,800
- I'm just saying it... - You want to see what it's like?

1784
01:05:36,800 --> 01:05:38,440
- because you said you would. - Sure.

1785
01:05:38,440 --> 01:05:41,480
- I'm just saying. - Gosh.

1786
01:05:43,440 --> 01:05:45,050
I'm just saying.

1787
01:05:45,410 --> 01:05:46,410
Don't worry about it.

1788
01:05:46,410 --> 01:05:47,550
- It's nothing. - I think I'm hyperventilating.

1789
01:05:47,550 --> 01:05:50,720
No. If there are any leftovers,

1790
01:05:50,720 --> 01:05:51,750
I'll happily try them.

1791
01:05:52,820 --> 01:05:55,390
I told her I was actually looking forward to having some tteokbokki.

1792
01:05:55,390 --> 01:05:57,160
(The part-timer has her wrapped around her fingers.)

1793
01:05:57,890 --> 01:06:00,930
Sorry. I was just kidding. It was a joke.

1794
01:06:01,860 --> 01:06:03,100
(Unlike the shocked boss,)

1795
01:06:03,100 --> 01:06:04,170
That was funny.

1796
01:06:04,170 --> 01:06:05,200
(Mimi calmly takes action.)

1797
01:06:05,200 --> 01:06:08,200
- Mimi. - Try this. It's really good.

1798
01:06:11,110 --> 01:06:12,710
(The intense reaction makes her proud.)

1799
01:06:12,710 --> 01:06:15,510
She soothed her with some fries.

1800
01:06:15,640 --> 01:06:17,850
(Fortunately, her request to try the food is fulfilled.)

1801
01:06:18,050 --> 01:06:20,050
Gabee, have you tried the pomegranate ade?

1802
01:06:20,050 --> 01:06:21,980
- Yes, I have. - I gave her the deep-fried shrimp.

1803
01:06:21,980 --> 01:06:23,180
You have. And the shrimp too.

1804
01:06:23,180 --> 01:06:25,890
The dishes I haven't tried are the burgers...

1805
01:06:25,890 --> 01:06:26,990
(Burgers and...)

1806
01:06:26,990 --> 01:06:29,260
- and tteokbokki. - They're the main dishes.

1807
01:06:29,820 --> 01:06:30,860
I can't describe the dish...

1808
01:06:30,860 --> 01:06:32,430
- to the customers. - Right.

1809
01:06:32,760 --> 01:06:34,530
- I can't tell them, "It's good." - Because you don't know.

1810
01:06:34,760 --> 01:06:37,230
- I got it. - But it's okay.

1811
01:06:37,230 --> 01:06:38,330
I'm really okay.

1812
01:06:38,770 --> 01:06:39,970
(Exhausted)

1813
01:06:40,200 --> 01:06:42,770
I'll cook them for you no matter what. Please wait.

1814
01:06:42,870 --> 01:06:45,170
- It's perfectly seasoned. - It's tasty, right?

1815
01:06:45,740 --> 01:06:47,380
- Nice. - It's really tasty.

1816
01:06:47,380 --> 01:06:48,440
It's really tasty, isn't it?

1817
01:06:48,740 --> 01:06:49,810
It's so good.

1818
01:06:49,810 --> 01:06:52,050
I see. When you said pomegranate ade, did you mean...

1819
01:06:52,510 --> 01:06:55,980
- zesty pomegranate ade? - Zesty pomegranate ade?

1820
01:06:55,980 --> 01:06:57,050
Goodness. That's right.

1821
01:06:58,350 --> 01:07:00,120
- Too much rice cake in a burger - Too much rice cake in a burger

1822
01:07:00,220 --> 01:07:02,720
- Patty slid in - Patty slid in

1823
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:03,790
(It's almost a duet now.)

1824
01:07:03,790 --> 01:07:04,830
- We'll get one of those. - Okay.

1825
01:07:04,830 --> 01:07:07,900
Hello. Would you like to take a look around the pop-up store first?

1826
01:07:08,160 --> 01:07:10,400
(The customers are rushing in,)

1827
01:07:10,870 --> 01:07:13,200
Please place this on your table.

1828
01:07:13,200 --> 01:07:14,300
(but they lead them professionally.)

1829
01:07:14,570 --> 01:07:17,070
You can take the utensils on the second floor.

1830
01:07:17,070 --> 01:07:18,270
Thank you.

1831
01:07:19,170 --> 01:07:20,210
Are you working part-time?

1832
01:07:20,210 --> 01:07:22,710
Yes. I'm helping them a bit today.

1833
01:07:23,080 --> 01:07:26,310
(Of course, the part-timer is also earning her deep-fried shrimp.)

1834
01:07:26,510 --> 01:07:28,380
- These are the bottoms. - Okay.

1835
01:07:28,380 --> 01:07:29,420
(The kitchen team is organizing the grilled rice cake buns.)

1836
01:07:30,080 --> 01:07:32,820
- That's the last batch of buns. - We need to cut more of them, then.

1837
01:07:32,820 --> 01:07:34,660
No, we just need to do it again.

1838
01:07:35,360 --> 01:07:37,290
Please let there be more than five.

1839
01:07:37,290 --> 01:07:38,830
There will be more than five buns when I open it.

1840
01:07:40,060 --> 01:07:41,130
- Why? - I'm okay.

1841
01:07:42,230 --> 01:07:44,430
- I'm happy. - You're happy.

1842
01:07:44,530 --> 01:07:46,230
- We have an order. - Okay.

1843
01:07:46,230 --> 01:07:48,170
We have 1 pizza, 1 tteokbokki,

1844
01:07:48,170 --> 01:07:49,240
and a beef burger.

1845
01:07:49,400 --> 01:07:52,470
For Table 7, 3 beef burgers, and 1 shrimp burger.

1846
01:07:52,470 --> 01:07:54,180
Also, 1 tteokbokki and 1 pizza.

1847
01:07:54,410 --> 01:07:57,750
Table 9 ordered 1 pizza, 1 tteokbokki, and 1 shrimp burger.

1848
01:07:57,750 --> 01:07:59,380
- Okay. - Because we're out of the buns,

1849
01:07:59,380 --> 01:08:01,020
the burgers might take some time.

1850
01:08:01,020 --> 01:08:02,050
Okay.

1851
01:08:02,050 --> 01:08:04,390
(Burger Order Status: 4 beef burgers and 2 shrimp burgers)

1852
01:08:04,620 --> 01:08:05,890
(However,)

1853
01:08:06,150 --> 01:08:08,390
(they only have 5 rice cake buns left.)

1854
01:08:08,960 --> 01:08:10,790
I really have to do that after doing this.

1855
01:08:11,360 --> 01:08:12,430
I need to work on the buns.

1856
01:08:13,060 --> 01:08:14,700
I have no choice now.

1857
01:08:15,400 --> 01:08:17,260
We have...

1858
01:08:17,260 --> 01:08:19,270
no choice now.

1859
01:08:20,130 --> 01:08:22,470
You think I can't pull it off. You think I'll fail, don't you?

1860
01:08:22,700 --> 01:08:23,840
(Laughing)

1861
01:08:24,040 --> 01:08:26,010
- No, we don't think so. - She's funny.

1862
01:08:27,640 --> 01:08:28,710
You think I'll fail.

1863
01:08:29,280 --> 01:08:30,680
I won't fail. I'm Lee Young Ji.

1864
01:08:31,210 --> 01:08:33,210
- Pizza was served. - We'll craft one beef burger first.

1865
01:08:33,210 --> 01:08:35,150
- Okay. - Nice.

1866
01:08:35,150 --> 01:08:36,650
- I'll cook three beef burgers now. - Okay.

1867
01:08:36,650 --> 01:08:37,690
(Chef Mimi takes over.)

1868
01:08:38,250 --> 01:08:40,290
- One beef burger is ready. - Okay.

1869
01:08:40,290 --> 01:08:42,260
It'll be great to serve the burger with tteokbokki.

1870
01:08:42,460 --> 01:08:45,490
- One shrimp burger is ready too. - Okay.

1871
01:08:46,290 --> 01:08:48,530
(Burger Order Status: Complete)

1872
01:08:48,800 --> 01:08:51,300
(3 rice cake buns are left.)

1873
01:08:51,670 --> 01:08:53,770
Young Ji, you really have to work on the buns after this.

1874
01:08:55,300 --> 01:08:57,070
We have 3 orders of pizza, which is 1st.

1875
01:08:57,070 --> 01:08:59,710
Let's make 3 pizzas. I've never made 3 burgers either.

1876
01:09:00,440 --> 01:09:01,540
Let's do this.

1877
01:09:01,540 --> 01:09:03,940
Three burgers? Don't worry. I'm here for you.

1878
01:09:04,250 --> 01:09:05,510
I'm making pizza all day.

1879
01:09:05,510 --> 01:09:06,850
(Making a large quantity as the business flourishes)

1880
01:09:07,750 --> 01:09:08,820
She's the pizza lady.

1881
01:09:08,820 --> 01:09:10,080
(A generously big pizza)

1882
01:09:11,150 --> 01:09:12,220
I'll push them down.

1883
01:09:12,220 --> 01:09:13,290
(Pressing down the patties)

1884
01:09:13,290 --> 01:09:14,320
I flip them.

1885
01:09:14,320 --> 01:09:15,560
(When the strangely flat patties are grilled,)

1886
01:09:15,560 --> 01:09:17,120
We'll make large patties now.

1887
01:09:17,360 --> 01:09:20,430
(pizzas are baked just in time.)

1888
01:09:20,830 --> 01:09:21,860
It's heavy.

1889
01:09:23,700 --> 01:09:24,770
It's hot.

1890
01:09:27,070 --> 01:09:28,600
Gosh. Nice.

1891
01:09:28,600 --> 01:09:30,700
(On the hot pizza,)

1892
01:09:31,110 --> 01:09:32,340
(she places basil before slicing it.)

1893
01:09:32,340 --> 01:09:33,440
Three beef burgers, right?

1894
01:09:33,840 --> 01:09:36,040
Pizza is getting smaller.

1895
01:09:36,980 --> 01:09:38,910
- It's true. - The dough...

1896
01:09:40,210 --> 01:09:41,650
- It's okay. - The dough was uneven.

1897
01:09:41,650 --> 01:09:42,820
(Don't get them wrong. They all weigh the same.)

1898
01:09:42,820 --> 01:09:44,790
- Sorry. - It's a bit small indeed.

1899
01:09:44,790 --> 01:09:46,590
(It's a bit small.)

1900
01:09:46,850 --> 01:09:49,060
(Yu Jin makes a turn.)

1901
01:09:50,120 --> 01:09:51,790
It's all up to our chef.

1902
01:09:53,690 --> 01:09:57,030
Here are your pizza and burger.

1903
01:09:57,300 --> 01:09:59,330
Here's your pizza.

1904
01:10:00,570 --> 01:10:03,200
Here's your pizza. I tried one before.

1905
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:04,270
- It's so good. - Is it?

1906
01:10:04,270 --> 01:10:05,610
It can be a bit spicy.

1907
01:10:05,610 --> 01:10:07,580
But it's deliciously spicy.

1908
01:10:08,240 --> 01:10:10,950
(She takes a big bite while holding a slice.)

1909
01:10:12,210 --> 01:10:13,310
(Laughing)

1910
01:10:13,510 --> 01:10:14,550
- Does it taste good? - Yes.

1911
01:10:15,750 --> 01:10:18,290
(Stretching)

1912
01:10:18,550 --> 01:10:20,250
The cheese is totally...

1913
01:10:22,390 --> 01:10:26,890
(It may be small in size, but it's super chewy.)

1914
01:10:27,290 --> 01:10:30,200
- Is Tabasco making it spicy? - Yes.

1915
01:10:30,200 --> 01:10:31,200
Anything else special?

1916
01:10:31,800 --> 01:10:32,870
- This is fun. - Can I go upstairs?

1917
01:10:32,870 --> 01:10:33,870
- It's all right, isn't it? - Yes.

1918
01:10:33,870 --> 01:10:35,300
(The part-timer laughs in a high pitch more frequently.)

1919
01:10:35,900 --> 01:10:37,370
- This is fun. - Yes.

1920
01:10:37,370 --> 01:10:39,270
- So far. - So far.

1921
01:10:39,270 --> 01:10:40,910
- Yes. So far. - So far.

1922
01:10:40,910 --> 01:10:41,910
(Her body and mind are out of sync.)

1923
01:10:42,410 --> 01:10:44,280
- Three beef patties are ready. - Okay.

1924
01:10:44,280 --> 01:10:47,410
(Patties are ready.)

1925
01:10:49,520 --> 01:10:51,820
(She piles up a tower of burgers.)

1926
01:10:52,120 --> 01:10:54,620
- Three beef burgers are ready. - Okay.

1927
01:10:55,760 --> 01:10:57,320
(Burger Order Status)

1928
01:10:57,320 --> 01:10:59,090
(All complete except for a shrimp burger)

1929
01:10:59,360 --> 01:11:01,200
(0 rice cake buns are left.)

1930
01:11:01,430 --> 01:11:05,000
(She starts cleaning the grill.)

1931
01:11:05,330 --> 01:11:07,770
That's our chef. Let's go.

1932
01:11:07,770 --> 01:11:09,700
- It's smoking like crazy. - Gosh.

1933
01:11:09,700 --> 01:11:11,370
It's crazy. Yes.

1934
01:11:11,370 --> 01:11:13,540
- Add the butter beneath the buns. - Should I do it?

1935
01:11:13,810 --> 01:11:16,010
Let them slide like this.

1936
01:11:16,310 --> 01:11:18,750
It's just like the buns sold near Gongdeok Station.

1937
01:11:19,480 --> 01:11:21,550
(Yu Jin in the meantime...)

1938
01:11:23,020 --> 01:11:24,890
- How was it? - It was really good.

1939
01:11:24,890 --> 01:11:25,950
- Really? - Why are you so good at this?

1940
01:11:26,290 --> 01:11:28,160
- Really? I'll let them know. - Yes.

1941
01:11:28,420 --> 01:11:30,660
- I'll tell them. Thanks. Good luck. - Travel safely. Okay.

1942
01:11:31,090 --> 01:11:35,530
(Table 7, 3 beef burger combos)

1943
01:11:35,530 --> 01:11:38,130
Here are your beef burgers.

1944
01:11:42,270 --> 01:11:44,810
(Crashing)

1945
01:11:45,040 --> 01:11:46,070
- Are you okay? - I'm sorry.

1946
01:11:46,070 --> 01:11:47,070
- It can happen. - Sorry.

1947
01:11:47,070 --> 01:11:48,540
- We'll bring a new one right away. - It can happen.

1948
01:11:48,940 --> 01:11:52,180
(Holding her breath and diving to the floor)

1949
01:11:55,020 --> 01:11:57,350
- Are you all right? - Yes, I am. I'm sorry.

1950
01:11:57,350 --> 01:11:59,820
- I'll wipe it quickly. - We'll get you a new one.

1951
01:11:59,820 --> 01:12:00,950
(Table 7, 1 crashed beef burger combo)

1952
01:12:01,290 --> 01:12:02,320
She's exhausted.

1953
01:12:02,320 --> 01:12:04,360
(Puppy Yu Jin, who created a mess, grabs cleaning tools...)

1954
01:12:04,960 --> 01:12:09,200
(and wipes the floor.)

1955
01:12:09,430 --> 01:12:11,700
Okay. Let's see. I'll be gentle.

1956
01:12:11,700 --> 01:12:12,970
(Young Ji, who has no idea,)

1957
01:12:13,700 --> 01:12:14,770
Not bad.

1958
01:12:14,770 --> 01:12:15,870
(is scratching the grill.)

1959
01:12:15,870 --> 01:12:16,900
Not bad.

1960
01:12:17,370 --> 01:12:18,440
Not bad.

1961
01:12:18,440 --> 01:12:19,510
(Burger Order Status)

1962
01:12:19,510 --> 01:12:22,410
(Beef burger, RIP)

1963
01:12:22,640 --> 01:12:23,640
Not bad.

1964
01:12:23,980 --> 01:12:26,380
(And the rice cake buns are still getting cooked.)

1965
01:12:26,380 --> 01:12:28,050
Overall, they're not bad.

1966
01:12:30,080 --> 01:12:32,150
- It was so good. Really. - It's delicious, right?

1967
01:12:32,590 --> 01:12:34,250
- What's with you? - I know.

1968
01:12:35,120 --> 01:12:36,190
Why are you so good?

1969
01:12:36,190 --> 01:12:38,190
- Is she your girlfriend? - She's my staff.

1970
01:12:38,190 --> 01:12:39,730
- Come on. - Come on. Stop lying.

1971
01:12:39,730 --> 01:12:41,300
- What's the point? - His eyes are... What?

1972
01:12:41,300 --> 01:12:43,200
- Are you two in a situationship? - She's an employee.

1973
01:12:43,200 --> 01:12:45,270
- Come on. - She works at my restaurant.

1974
01:12:45,800 --> 01:12:47,600
- The food was good, right? - You're really good at this.

1975
01:12:47,740 --> 01:12:49,640
- Really? Give us some feedback. - It was good.

1976
01:12:50,070 --> 01:12:52,040
Honestly, I have no complaints. Really.

1977
01:12:52,040 --> 01:12:53,040
(You're good on your own now.)

1978
01:12:53,140 --> 01:12:54,410
Honestly, I thought it wouldn't taste good,

1979
01:12:54,410 --> 01:12:55,710
- so I only ordered 2 dishes. - Right. You ordered 2.

1980
01:12:55,710 --> 01:12:57,850
You ordered only two dishes, thinking they wouldn't taste good.

1981
01:12:57,850 --> 01:12:59,680
- I was shocked by how tasty it was. - Other dishes are tasty too.

1982
01:12:59,680 --> 01:13:01,150
You should have some more.

1983
01:13:01,150 --> 01:13:03,950
You should've ordered more for us. Why did you order just a little?

1984
01:13:04,050 --> 01:13:06,020
No. I didn't want to trouble you.

1985
01:13:06,720 --> 01:13:09,490
- I see. You're so kind. - Thank you, by the way.

1986
01:13:09,490 --> 01:13:11,360
Are we on par with Viatoledo?

1987
01:13:12,490 --> 01:13:14,960
It's possible if you try a little harder.

1988
01:13:15,060 --> 01:13:17,500
- Look how fast you work. - It's not bad, is it?

1989
01:13:18,070 --> 01:13:20,770
- It's not bad at all. - I'm really sorry, Young Ji.

1990
01:13:20,770 --> 01:13:22,700
- Did you knock it over? - I knocked it over.

1991
01:13:23,370 --> 01:13:25,770
- What? - The burger. You haven't heard.

1992
01:13:26,140 --> 01:13:28,410
- I haven't. - I went overboard...

1993
01:13:28,410 --> 01:13:29,440
and carried three burgers.

1994
01:13:29,440 --> 01:13:31,080
- And I knocked over one of them. - Are you hurt?

1995
01:13:31,080 --> 01:13:32,210
- No, I'm totally fine. - Okay.

1996
01:13:32,710 --> 01:13:34,750
You're so sweet. Thank you. I'm sorry.

1997
01:13:35,480 --> 01:13:36,580
How mature of you.

1998
01:13:36,980 --> 01:13:38,020
What do you say? I was a good boyfriend.

1999
01:13:39,090 --> 01:13:41,090
I actually wanted...

2000
01:13:41,860 --> 01:13:44,090
to flick on Yu Jin's head, but I remained a good boyfriend.

2001
01:13:44,760 --> 01:13:46,790
- Anyway, good luck. I'll get going. - Okay. Take care.

2002
01:13:46,790 --> 01:13:47,800
Thank you.

2003
01:13:47,900 --> 01:13:49,760
Thank you. It's all thanks to you.

2004
01:13:49,860 --> 01:13:52,700
- You can do this, Gabee. - Bye.

2005
01:13:53,600 --> 01:13:54,840
That was a lie. It's all thanks to me.

2006
01:13:56,040 --> 01:13:58,970
(She's kidding. Thank you for your help, Manager Kwon.)

2007
01:13:59,170 --> 01:14:01,510
Yu Jin, did you let them see you fall?

2008
01:14:01,710 --> 01:14:03,440
Come on. I showed them all right.

2009
01:14:03,440 --> 01:14:05,410
- Did you show them? Good job, then. - Yes.

2010
01:14:05,580 --> 01:14:06,850
Then one more beef burger, Yu Jin?

2011
01:14:07,280 --> 01:14:09,480
Yes. We need 1 beef burger and 1 shrimp burger.

2012
01:14:09,480 --> 01:14:11,850
- Sorry. That's right. - Right? One more beef burger.

2013
01:14:11,890 --> 01:14:13,720
(Coming up next)

2014
01:14:14,090 --> 01:14:17,860
(Space Rice Cake is in chaos again today.)

2015
01:14:18,460 --> 01:14:20,730
(I'm crying.)

2016
01:14:20,990 --> 01:14:24,800
(In the end, the head chef ends up flat on the floor.)

2017
01:14:25,370 --> 01:14:26,530
(Appearing before exhausted Earth Arcaders...)

2018
01:14:28,570 --> 01:14:29,640
Good morning. What?

2019
01:14:30,070 --> 01:14:31,470
(is the third part-timer of Space Rice Cake.)

2020
01:14:31,710 --> 01:14:33,410
- Kyung Soo. - Hello, Young Ji.

2021
01:14:34,580 --> 01:14:38,780
(Doh Kyung Soo, the director of KKPP Food)

2022
01:14:39,650 --> 01:14:44,420
(With a professional, the kitchen finally settles down.)

2023
01:14:44,420 --> 01:14:45,790
(You'd better not mess it up.)

2024
01:14:46,050 --> 01:14:48,460
(Director, I won't let you down.)

2025
01:14:49,020 --> 01:14:52,760
(A director who's got both charisma and sweetness)

2026
01:14:52,930 --> 01:14:55,500
(Being next to you makes my heart flutter.)

2027
01:14:55,700 --> 01:14:59,570
(Space Rice Cake just got a whole lot sweeter.)

2028
01:14:59,570 --> 01:15:01,600
(The secret dish he's here to teach them)

2029
01:15:01,770 --> 01:15:03,400
(On top of crispy rice crackers)

2030
01:15:03,600 --> 01:15:07,570
(Exotic ingredients to bring in more flavor)

2031
01:15:07,740 --> 01:15:10,110
(Rice cracker tacos)

2032
01:15:10,310 --> 01:15:12,050
(It's delicious.)

2033
01:15:12,080 --> 01:15:14,450
(A unique charm that draws in not only the Earth Arcaders...)

2034
01:15:14,680 --> 01:15:18,390
(but also the customers)

2035
01:15:18,620 --> 01:15:21,590
(Kicking off the service with confidence)

2036
01:15:21,720 --> 01:15:23,760
(Or so we thought...)

2037
01:15:24,190 --> 01:15:25,190
(Didn't they order tacos?)

2038
01:15:25,190 --> 01:15:27,060
(I forgot to put them in.)

2039
01:15:27,790 --> 01:15:30,100
(Young Ji, I ruined one. I'm sorry.)

2040
01:15:31,730 --> 01:15:33,670
(Hey, Kyung Soo)

2041
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:38,610
(Mistake after mistake right from the start)

2042
01:15:38,910 --> 01:15:41,880
(The Earth Arcaders get betrayed by the person they trusted.)

2043
01:15:41,940 --> 01:15:43,180
I'm the worst.

2044
01:15:43,180 --> 01:15:44,540
(What fate awaits part-timer Do Kyung Soo?)

2045
01:15:44,540 --> 01:15:51,750
(What fate awaits part-timer Do Kyung Soo?)

2046
01:15:59,830 --> 01:16:01,400
(Space Rice Cake)
